{"total_count":23,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1263","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1263/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1263/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1263/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1263","id":6271906406,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABddWyZg","number":1263,"title":"Rifamycin grounding method still claims an exact label match after contextual family review","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-08T14:25:17Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T15:50:06Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Independent full companion review found a method-provenance defect in `data/ingredients/mapped/Rifamycin.yaml`, SHA256 `0319c48944ab91a2af53000f5e7488646224cf4683c327a2839ba6d56c8a2a8e`: `ontology_mapping.mapping_quality` remains `EXACT_MATCH`, although the actual evidence documents a contextual choice of the rifamycin family.\n\nThe preferred/source label is singular `Rifamycin`; [ChEBI:26580](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:26580) has primary label `rifamycins` and singular `rifamycin` as a synonym. [ChEBI:29673](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:29673), rifamycin SV, also carries that synonym. MAPPING_SEMANTICS section0 defines EXACT_MATCH as primary-label resolution and requires a unique synonym resolution for SYNONYM_MATCH. The owner's September23 history and CURATOR_JUDGMENT evidence instead document deliberate family-level re-grounding.\n\nPreserve the explicit #760 decision: bare Rifamycin remains CHEBI:26580, the three original MicrobeDecoder observations remain at family scope, and Rifamycin_Sv remains separately CHEBI:29673. Assign no family CAS, molecular structure, supplier formulation or inference of production/resistance for every family member. The independently reviewed complete scoped mapping claim remains supported; this finding does not invalidate its family identity or authorize a different predicate.\n\nThe bounded correction should record the method actually performed, using MANUAL_CURATION with truthful agent-assisted evidence and append-only history, while preserving prior evidence/history, identity, occurrences and scientific holds. Do not substitute SYNONYM_MATCH merely to make the string agree, imply human verification, or transplant stale owner-bound support. Use existing guarded source/publication writers, meaningful regression coverage and fresh exact-owner/complete-row independent review. Regenerate dependent native products when required. Until delivered, the method field must remain explicitly unapproved and this issue stays open.\n\nFinding `F51-CHEM-001` was independently confirmed by `worker04:/root/correction_chemistry`, `worker04:/root/assembly_review` and the coordinator before any source correction. Exact local evidence: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/workers/w04/worktree/.temp/full51-prospective-scientific-review-v1/science-chemistry/findings.json`, SHA256 `d848af501e5bd6d862dfeb68793e8d11ad54bfd31c0121ed8f6da2356bab1afc`. The complete review packet is still being sealed; this filing binds the already inspected finding and primary captures, not a future seal.\n\nPrimary ChEBI API captures: 26580 SHA256 `7deff2d6075d5344c25df1cca36166ecf161bff7a4ccb564df9bb54c41444529`, retrieved 2026-11-08T06:11:12.405578Z; 29673 SHA256 `36bc675b19e32e24ea1d5fda368458471925ece8b74208ae232c7879ae6ff6fa`, retrieved 2026-11-08T06:11:12.711699Z. The coordinator rehashed/read both bodies and the current owner, and read #760, #1222 and #1258 with their comments. All-state Rifamycin searches returned seven issues and four PRs; none tracks this method defect. The exact finding search returned zero. Deduplication receipts are under `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/rifamycin-method-finding-dedup-v1/`.\n\nThis is an ancillary finding, separate from the frozen 1,879 source cases and the unchanged 934-operation draft. No owner, claim, source input or export was changed by this filing.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1263/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1263/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1258","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1258/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1258/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1258/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1258","id":6271125976,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdcnJ2A","number":1258,"title":"Xanthine retains CAS_RN_LOOKUP despite a shared CAS across ChEBI tautomers","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-11-08T12:54:14Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T15:46:57Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Independent full companion review found a confirmed method-provenance defect in `data/ingredients/mapped/Xanthine.yaml` (SHA256 `c72c948fb793dd36ba53def8a77230d0ac337bec0962369f01c6e29848bccd22`). The current `ontology_mapping.mapping_quality` is `CAS_RN_LOOKUP`, but primary ChEBI records for both [9H-xanthine / CHEBI:17712](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:17712) and [7H-xanthine / CHEBI:48517](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:48517) carry CAS 69-89-6. MAPPING_SEMANTICS section0 requires a unique CAS-to-target resolution for that grade. A shared CAS cannot establish it.\n\nPreserve the actual prior decision in #760: the existing ingredient representation remains CHEBI:17712 / CAS69-89-6, generic traits use CHEBI:15318, and neither standard InChI nor unqualified recipe names establish tautomer-pure reagent identity. The complete existing mapping row explicitly uses `semapv:ManualMappingCuration`; independent review still supports that bounded row and the qualified registry annotation. The finding concerns the owner's claimed selection method, not permission to choose a different tautomer, merge owners or infer physical purity.\n\nDeduplication read all-state Xanthine and CAS-method results and the full #760 decision. #1201 contains separate source-shard method/completeness cases; it does not already track this unchanged companion owner. This issue is filed before any correction.\n\nA bounded correction must record the method actually performed under the accepted scope decision, preserve the original CAS lookup/history as historical evidence, append truthful curation history, and keep the exact identity, source occurrences, aliases and role/export holds. Do not mechanically substitute EXACT_MATCH or SYNONYM_MATCH: both terms also carry the name Xanthine. Verify whether the native manual method contract expresses the performed review without inventing human verification; if a further scientific ruling is truly needed, document the precise choice and retain the hold. Use the guarded writer, meaningful regression coverage, native synchronization/SSSOM and independent exact-byte re-review before publication.\n\nEvidence: worker09's immutable `final-companion-candidate-review-v2` under `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/workers/w09/worktree/.temp/`; finding `FC2-XANTHINE-METHOD-001`, severity major/native P2. Manifest SHA256 `003ddab328359fbaeff063749e0d1ddce4ffe55ba58733894e55b0572f6ac204`; machine findings SHA256 `ef5bc622e1abf990f2304378621aa32c35f22b83ab824a9e3e6fe52b57e4fdcc`. Primary captures SHA256 `2aa1bf444738308831318e577ae7e6a0fed981702348d6ccc35ae3eb06f44e60` and `b6c12c0f7b903706701f57b7291e6dd4fc3e7f886127d77ee8092729f45e0cc5`, retaining their original 2026-11-08 retrieval times. Distinct chemistry and skeptical reviewers agreed; root rehashed the complete553-member packet and read both source CAS lists. No source or export correction has been applied.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1258/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1258/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1227","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1227/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1227/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1227/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1227","id":6268624337,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdaOd0Q","number":1227,"title":"Correct Worker08 source scope, completeness, identity and provenance findings","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:13:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T11:03:11Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Independent review of Worker08’s published `b90a2fd4681d20e2586481b7b9b1114a78281b94` found bounded corrections in isolated proposals. Maintained owners/canonical mappings have not been changed by this review. The complete source assessment has188 cases and113 selected payloads;94 affected payloads are a union across findings, not94 chemical rejections.\n\nThe frozen external review is `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/workers/w03/worktree/.temp/w08-published-head-independent-review-v1/`: findings SHA256 `11e3681d90be88d52a309fc6ed301bcb4c37c749ffb144640175cea6db501af5`, full manifest `9b34903748fba1da78b5649ad471a1804da04a78b7775004d71f6b8d36f8cf76`. Coordinator triage independently verified all5070 manifest members and all113 exact Git payloads; its action matrix SHA256 is `9a26d2adf42df8195f19b2090754978db063dfe515f8738a2a54f9d4c3f772f4`. Original findings, drafts, captures and reviews remain immutable.\n\nThis tracker covers the following seven remaining W08 groups. W08-IR-001 belongs to1226, IR-003/004 to1201, IR-008 to811 and IR-010 to1210; those scopes are not duplicated here.1173 tracks Worker01 lineage, and718 is broader context rather than this correction ledger.\n\n| Finding | Confirmed defect | Bounded correction |\n|---|---|---|\n| W08-IR-002 | JCM403 numbered pointers remain global resolving labels | Qualify preferred terms with JCM and preparation identity; preserve exact old pointer strings and all source provenance as REJECTED_LABEL; retain source occurrence routing and append history. Re-review exact successor and all backlinks; do not resolve generic pointers by label alone. |\n| W08-IR-005 | Retained supernatant water inference uses literal transcription method | Use CURATED_INTERPRETATION for the water-retention inference with explicit rationale and unmeasured retained-salt limits, or omit the derived has-part list until supported. Preserve all charge recipe facts in provenance and do not convert them into retained concentrations. Ground the water component if retained. |\n| W08-IR-006 | Component completeness does not consistently follow source-relative enum meanings | For each precisely identified assertion, distinguish explicit omitted constituents (PARTIAL), source-unestablished closure (UNKNOWN), and complete source enumeration (COMPLETE). Missing concentration, final volume, titrant quantity or molecular grounding alone does not determine membership completeness. Preserve the bounded stock and all unknowns. |\n| W08-IR-007 | Nalidixic-acid occurrence applicability lacks readable primary support | Bind a readable exact NBRC1314 primary capture or record that occurrence as source-held/unverified while retaining the independently supported acid candidate. Keep the successful1301 capture separate from failed1314/M2023 requests; do not claim an unread source was inspected. |\n| W08-IR-009 | Trypticase soy broth mapping grade overstates primary-label match | Change mapping_quality to SYNONYM_MATCH with a truthful history event and preserve correct identifier, canonical ontology label, mixture components and own-identifier exact SSSOM semantics. |\n| W08-IR-011 | Allen phosphate remaining requirement repeats a resolved dose distinction | Narrow case63 remaining requirement to unusual seven-water supplied-form confirmation or correction, and state the source-resolved5ml dose transcription separately. Preserve the chemical hold and frozen input. |\n| W08-IR-012 | L-asparagine monohydrate retains parent treatment despite exact NCIT evidence | Adjudicate NCIT:C87433 against its exact L-hydrate synonym and CAS5794-13-8 under section3 exact-term priority, updating primary identifier and mapping grade where supported. Preserve the CAS/source alias/history and distinguish DL hydrate. Separately clarify or verify stereochemical SMILES scope without inventing a structure or calling an unspecified SMILES a racemate. |\n\nThe completeness correction requires source-specific judgment. The native enum means COMPLETE only when the cited source establishes the retained constituent list; PARTIAL means the source identifies omitted constituents; UNKNOWN means closure is not established. Missing amount, final volume, hydration, stereochemistry or a catalog CURIE is not an omitted constituent.\n\nThe external final reviewer identified29 unsupported PARTIAL assertions among34, excluding five rather than rewriting them all. Independent coordinator source-table readback refines five of those29: the two PCR-S11 phosphate stock recipes, Allen phosphate stock, MediaDive552 “5.0g in100ml H2O” preparation, and JCM941 Solution C explicitly enumerate their two retained inputs. COMPLETE is recommended for that literal input-list scope, preserving all chemical-form and physical-composition uncertainty; the other24 uncertain lists warrant UNKNOWN. The five exclusions remain separately assessed (YPS omitted literal inputs; PCR buffer and JCM628/629 pH/CO2 treatment). Do not invent titrants, carriers or gas quantities. The exact34-row table and original source hashes are in `completeness-adjudication-refinement.json` and `complete-list-primary-proof.json`.\n\nFor JCM403, actual primary formulation separates the six-input vitamin solution from the5mg B12/100ml distilled-water stock. Six provider-free pointer aliases resolve through native policy despite citation provenance. Qualify the preferred preparation names and preserve pointers as non-resolving provenance; registry promotion of the existing B12 placeholder is separately tracked under1201.\n\nFor NBRC1356 mineral base1, the source instructs use of the supernatant after precipitation. Retained water is an inference, so record CURATED_INTERPRETATION if retained, with UNKNOWN retained composition. Charged salt quantities must not become retained concentrations.\n\nFor nalidixic acid, independently readable NBRC1301 supports the acid/source claim; exact NBRC1314/TOGOM2023 applicability remains unavailable. Obtain readable primary evidence or hold only that occurrence. Source retrieval failure neither rejects the supported acid identity nor justifies claiming the failed source was read.\n\nFor L-asparagine monohydrate, the archived official NCIT:C87433 response (`54c71948e42aaa1995f271abc3cf70e4ccb9c7b6ae304fa1eff8d754a7af4dae`) records CAS5794-13-8, formula C4H8N2O3.H2O and exact synonym “L-Asparagine Monohydrate”. Under MAPPING_SEMANTICS§3, evaluate that exact target before retaining CAS-primary/NARROW_MATCH. Preserve the distinct DL hydrate. The non-isomeric SMILES does not itself assert racemization; do not invent a replacement structure. Any primary-ID change requires dependent-reference accounting and fresh content-bound review.\n\nOther small corrections retain sound chemistry: Trypticase soy broth is an exact synonym of the ontology’s preferred “tryptic soy broth”, so its actual lookup grade is SYNONYM_MATCH; the Allen stock dose is already resolved as5ml of a6g/L source stock, while the unusual seven-water supplied formula remains held.\n\nExact non-bulk targets follow. The29 completeness targets are fully listed in the attached action matrix rather than authorizing edits to every PARTIAL record.\n\n**JCM403 numbered pointers remain global resolving labels**\n\n| Proposal / owner | Exact payload SHA256 |\n|---|---|\n| `vm-prop-jcm403-b12` / `data/ingredients/unmapped/Vitamin_B12_Solution_See_Medium_No_403.yaml` | `94956716b71347bd431921e64a06ddd2593d6e7bc50e748e1be3c3cc78bb73a8` |\n| `vm-prop-jcm403-vitamin` / `data/ingredients/mapped/Vitamin_Solution_See_Medium_No_403.yaml` | `a86933326bed8cdf623c0a8dc41622bd6e3bc54243addf1610be4f884dda1db5` |\n\n**Retained supernatant water inference uses literal transcription method**\n\n| Proposal / owner | Exact payload SHA256 |\n|---|---|\n| `vm1201-prop-nbrc1356-mineral-base1` / `data/ingredients/mapped/NBRC1356_Mineral_Base1_Supernatant.yaml` | `0aa699c355adee9161a6778c5ee892e07d5f85b2cf90494dea6b31f9072f0256` |\n\n**Nalidixic-acid occurrence applicability lacks readable primary support**\n\n| Proposal / owner | Exact payload SHA256 |\n|---|---|\n| `op-nalidixic-new` / `data/ingredients/mapped/Nalidixic_Acid.yaml` | `ca0acf4743b49628c9a2086a412abbc2c82840367a40251061e8b43608b50d72` |\n\n**Trypticase soy broth mapping grade overstates primary-label match**\n\n| Proposal / owner | Exact payload SHA256 |\n|---|---|\n| `op1201-trypticase-soy-broth` / `data/ingredients/unmapped/Trypticase_Soy_Broth.yaml` | `cbc788c1a9ce7cea22a92b4360bad7c113f0e99c2cf5a1ecbbd3a0e79f99aa6c` |\n\n**L-asparagine monohydrate retains parent treatment despite exact NCIT evidence**\n\n| Proposal / owner | Exact payload SHA256 |\n|---|---|\n| `op-l-asn-hydrate-alias` / `data/ingredients/mapped/L-Asparagine_Monohydrate.yaml` | `07d8b55d6773f4e16ad57e18e5ed72a4438bdeb207cdfb435da84cc2cb62e20a` |\n\n\nExact affected `/component_assertion/completeness` entries (all currently PARTIAL):\n\n| Proposal | Source-relative recommendation |\n|---|---|\n| `if1201-new-dsmz_trace_2n_naoh` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-jcm_1130_10n_naoh` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-atcc_nitrosolobus_6n_naoh` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-pcr_s11_01n_naoh` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-dsmz_104_8n_naoh` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-jcm_221_02n_naoh` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-wolin_mineral_05n_naoh` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-atcc_1340_naoh_4g_100ml` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-jcm_574_1m_kh2po4` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-jcm_574_1m_k2hpo4` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-pbbm_1m_na2hpo4` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-pcr_s11_50mm_nah2po4` | COMPLETE for the explicit literal two-input list |\n| `if1201-new-pcr_s11_50mm_na2hpo4` | COMPLETE for the explicit literal two-input list |\n| `if1201-new-allen_m2231_phosphate_stock` | COMPLETE for the explicit literal two-input list |\n| `if1201-new-jcm_908_sulfide_10pct_wv` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-jcm_713_sulfide_24pct` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-atcc_1943_sulfide_25pct` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-atcc_1942_sulfide_5pct` | UNKNOWN |\n| `if1201-new-mediadive_552_thiosulfate_5g_100ml` | COMPLETE for the explicit literal two-input list |\n| `if1201-new-jcm_941_solution_c` | COMPLETE for the explicit literal two-input list |\n| `op1201-r2a-medium` | UNKNOWN |\n| `op1201-amphotericin-stock` | UNKNOWN |\n| `vm1201-prop-nbrc1356-mineral-base1` | UNKNOWN |\n| `vm1201-prop-jcm515-b12-partial` | UNKNOWN |\n| `vm1201-prop-jcm647-b12-partial` | UNKNOWN |\n| `vm1201-prop-jcm1354-b12-partial` | UNKNOWN |\n| `vm1201-prop-atcc2883-b12-partial` | UNKNOWN |\n| `vm1201-prop-togo125-k1-partial` | UNKNOWN |\n| `vm1201-prop-dsm1245-k1-partial` | UNKNOWN |\n\nRequired follow-up: preserve beforeimages and historical/source evidence; make bounded successor proposals and exact case/evidence backlinks; bind a new complete manifest; obtain independent review of the final scientific payloads and native schema/partonomy/lineage checks. No maintained-data application, source-hold release, role/export approval, owner merge or cross-shard winner selection is authorized by this issue.\n\nDeduplication context: all-state title/body inventory and targeted current comments were read. Generic pedigree in718/1173 and the worker06-specific1217 findings do not already track these W08 payload corrections. The coordinator performs final live deduplication before filing.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1227/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1227/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1201","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1201/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1201/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1201/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1201","id":6268078705,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdZtKcQ","number":1201,"title":"Complete deferred source-qualified curation in final unmatched review shards","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":13,"created_at":"2026-11-08T05:47:07Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T08:44:52Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Final coordinator review of two published source-review shards found that several no-change outcomes defer already-authorized curation rather than identify a missing scientific fact. Worker04 head `0d2c73e5aee5adb88782537755472d9ca0c5c3cd`; worker08 head `7efd3f8b98f9e822431dcb510c2c242a2569cfc7`; both depend on #1158 at `e000d66`.\n\nConcrete examples:\n\n- Worker08 case `CM_NAME:b9a945a3356d0c885eea986a2f6223e78c8e7d7163ee95629061a640294cbbe8` (H2O deionized) correctly distinguishes deionization from distillation, but its remaining requirement is to perform native owner lookup and use or create the appropriately scoped owner. [DSMZ533](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium533.pdf) explicitly identifies deionized water in both main and trace stock. No proposal or completed lookup disposition accompanies that deferred step.\n- Worker08 case `CM_NAME:e69128522cfe555f63dd51d4a23ece86363290b3839180386b090f368b28d1cc` (glycine-NaOH buffer) preserves a source-defined concentration and pH, and correctly finds a receiving-medium volume transcription error. [JCM906](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=906) specifies the separately prepared buffer. The decision defers representing the stock without explaining which missing fact prevents a bounded preparation identity. It must not be equated to pure glycine or assigned invented titrant amounts.\n- Worker04 case `CM_NAME:2f91fab8feab468a33e48d01e2f0a1363b9ad70816766c69a1e8d68c0ed6f8d5` describes the [NBRC15](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=15) treated, clarified V-8 preparation but defers representing it until later curation. Lack of a molecular mapping or extraction yield does not by itself establish that a source-qualified preparation cannot be represented with an honest partial assertion.\n\nRelated outcomes defer normality-qualified NaOH stocks, source-specific top layers, C9322 supplied-form review, and malted wheat meal because an exact molecular/ontology mapping or later complete-owner review is absent. These are leads for reassessment, not predetermined identity approvals. Genuine solvent, formulation, provenance or supplied-form uncertainties may remain after primary research.\n\nReassess the full no-change cohorts against MAPPING_SEMANTICS sections3/6 and add-media. Complete supported proposal work, or state the precise scientific fact still missing and the actual primary-source searches. Keep receiving-medium dose/unit repair separate from ingredient identity. Never invent concentrations, solvent, chemistry, product equivalence, component completeness, or exact ontology matches; preserve all native holds and old review bytes. Require separate skeptical review of successor evidence/payloads and ordinary commits/pushes on the existing worker branches. No maintained data or export approval is requested from workers.\n\nThis extends the same class of completeness problem seen in #1163 and #1193 to distinct final shards; those earlier findings remain preserved. Exact frozen decisions and capture hashes are retained in the coordinator's immutable `w04-w08-deferred-curation-v1/review-inputs.json` and will accompany the campaign evidence. This is a review-completeness finding, not a statement that every listed source must map.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1201/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1201/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1234","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1234/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1234/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1234/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1234","id":6268673381,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdaRdZQ","number":1234,"title":"Remove unsupported supplier-prepoured scope from the Wilkins-Chalgren proposal","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:20:57Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T07:20:57Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The unapplied W04 new-owner payload Oxoid_Wilkins_Chalgren_Agar_Plates.yaml asserts a supplier-prepared basal plate product across its material scope, supplied form and evidence. PMC3101863 reports growth on Oxoid Wilkins-Chalgren agar plates supplemented with blood and antibiotics. It does not establish that basal plates were purchased pre-poured or the order of plate preparation.\n\nExact reviewed scope:\n- Finding `MEDIA-SCI-01`; stable key `w04-independent-MEDIA-SCI-01`; immutable peer review `20261108T070033Z-w04-successor-science-v1`.\n- `I1201-MEDIA-P-oxoid_wilkins_chalgren_agar_plates`; owner `data/ingredients/mapped/Oxoid_Wilkins_Chalgren_Agar_Plates.yaml`; before `absent (new proposal; no maintained owner created)`; proposed SHA256 `0554c990d6eaacdc7dfef4977d87fbb138998dd93eeb0b6fd509d15b793adc11`.\n  [Exact published proposal](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/successors/issue-1201-v1/proposals/media/Oxoid_Wilkins_Chalgren_Agar_Plates.yaml).\n\nCorrect only the unsupported procurement/preparation claim in every affected field, including preferred material scope, supplied form, notes, mapping evidence, curation history and recipe reference. Represent the source-supported agar/plate preparation with honest supplements and remaining limitations. Do not infer the opposite purchase form from a current powder catalogue comparator or treat blood/antibiotics as part of an unqualified basal supplier product. Preserve the old payload/evidence as a historical draft and publish a fully bound successor.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- [Primary/ontology source](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3101863/); capture SHA256 `0d6b310e7e41ca1501369512ae6b0958becc068381fbd72dccaa4166fb78c04d`; Methods: Bacterial Growth Conditions\n- [Primary/ontology source](https://www.thermofisher.com/order/catalog/product/CM0619B); capture SHA256 `4421686b2cbcab2344e98871108f7b71c26959c892fbfa7455212a106607e5a3`; ProductCM0619B current powder comparator, not historical procurement\n\nDeduplication: Fresh all-state Wilkins search found no exact tracker. #1201 is related source-completion context; this dedicated finding concerns an affirmative unsupported new-payload claim.\n\nReview context: W04 published head `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9`, frozen campaign base `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99`. Main as observed at `0dac278466699129a083343a921c2e0ca18a9ab4` has the same eighteen affected inherited-owner blobs as the frozen baseline; this is not a report of already-applied campaign curation. The full independent assembly covers 188 source cases and 115 proposals and remains `needs_curation`. Original peer review and evidence are immutable. Agent-authored new mapping evidence must satisfy #1226 without relabeling historical human evidence. The fix must use existing native guarded proposal validation and independent re-review; it grants no maintained-owner or export approval and requires no new gate, threshold, or synonym-selection rule.\n\n<!-- mim-review-round:20261108T071043Z-w04-final-scientific-issue-plan -->\n<!-- mim-review-bundle:wilkins-preparation -->\n<!-- mim-fingerprints:w04-independent-MEDIA-SCI-01 -->\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1234/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1234/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/753","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/753/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/753/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/753/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/753","id":5548928560,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABSr3uMA","number":753,"title":"Correct three supported CAS assertions with invalid check digits","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-09-23T04:50:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T01:26:48Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The kg-microbe #1123 name-disagreement review exposed an invalid Lysozyme CAS identifier. An arithmetic check of the current supported MIM candidate found three invalid CAS RNs:\n\n| Subject | Published target | Calculated check digit | Stored digit |\n| --- | --- | ---: | ---: |\n| MIM:Izalpinin | cas:480-14-4 | 8 | 4 |\n| MIM:Lysozyme | cas:2650-88-3 | 6 | 3 |\n| MIM:Methyl-2-Hydroxy-Phenylproprionate | cas:89471-28-0 | 3 | 0 |\n\nChecked against main `5019d6871fe0b0f47eccd50f9d0c169c98c40484` and the proposed #752 mapping-only follow-up. [CAS documents its check-digit method](https://www.cas.org/es-es/training/documentation/chemical-substances/checkdig): multiply the digits before the final check digit from right to left by 1, 2, ... and take the sum modulo 10. For Lysozyme, `8*1+8*2+0*3+5*4+6*5+2*6 = 86`, giving 6 rather than 3.\n\nA valid checksum does not establish chemical identity. Do not repair these by substituting the calculated digit: a missing or substituted earlier digit is also possible. Lysozyme needs source/form review, not forced equivalence with FOODON:03413135 merely to clear a downstream disagreement.\n\nImmediate containment: add exact row/owner-bound WITHHOLD decisions for these three CAS assertions while preserving the complete source payloads and unrelated local-identifier assertions. Historical/published release files stay immutable.\n\nRemaining acceptance: inspect original source records, independently verify the intended compounds/materials and replacement identifiers, correct YAML/SSSOM via the existing mapping-change receipt chain, and explicitly re-review corrected rows. Add a supported-release CAS check-digit gate to prevent recurrence without confusing syntactic validity with identity approval. This issue remains open until source correction and the permanent gate are complete.\n\nRelated: #752 and https://github.com/Knowledge-Graph-Hub/kg-microbe/issues/1123.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/753/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/753/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/268","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/268/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/268/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/268/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/268","id":5076761039,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABLpk5zw","number":268,"title":"AUTO_BACKFILL_CHEBI_CHEMISTRY propagates a wrong grounding into structure fields and can flip ingredient_type","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-08-06T01:43:33Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T07:23:23Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Found reviewing PR #266 (#263).\n\nAll four records re-grounded in #263 had `molecular_formula` / `inchi` / `smiles` (and one `pubchem_cid`) written onto them by `AUTO_BACKFILL_CHEBI_CHEMISTRY`, copied from the CHEBI term the record pointed at. When that term is wrong, the backfill silently manufactures wrong chemistry that looks curated.\n\n`Casamino acids` shows the worst of it. It is a casein hydrolysate — an undefined mixture — and was correctly typed `UNDEFINED_MIXTURE` by a rule matching the name. Then:\n\n1. The record was grounded to CHEBI:78020 *heptacosanoate* (wrong).\n2. `AUTO_BACKFILL_CHEBI_CHEMISTRY` wrote heptacosanoate's `C27H53O2` / InChI / SMILES onto it.\n3. `auto_classify_ingredient_type` saw populated chemical structure and **re-typed the record `SINGLE_INGREDIENT`**, overwriting the correct classification — its own history says *\"chemical structure populated (molecular_formula)\"*.\n\nSo one wrong id cascaded into wrong structure and a wrong record type, each step looking like a legitimate automated curation entry in `curation_history`. Nothing flagged the contradiction between `ingredient_type=UNDEFINED_MIXTURE` and \"has a single exact molecular formula\".\n\nWorth considering:\n- **Record provenance on backfilled fields.** If `molecular_formula` carried \"derived from `<curie>`\", re-grounding could invalidate it automatically instead of relying on a curator to notice. (#138 is the same shape: stale derived columns outranking corrections.)\n- **Do not let a derived field drive a classification.** `auto_classify_ingredient_type` promoting `UNDEFINED_MIXTURE` → `SINGLE_INGREDIENT` on the strength of a backfilled formula lets a grounding error rewrite the record's identity.\n- **Flag the contradiction.** A name matching a known complex/mixture pattern *and* a single exact formula is a signal worth surfacing.\n\nPR #266 drops the poisoned fields on the four affected records rather than recomputing them, but does not address the mechanism — any future wrong grounding will do this again.\n\nRelated: #263, #266, #138, #237.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/268/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/268/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1217","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1217/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1217/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1217/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1217","id":6268342296,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdZ9QGA","number":1217,"title":"Resolve worker06 independent source-scope, component-provenance and completeness findings","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-11-08T06:28:59Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T08:34:19Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Independent full-shard review of worker06 at `d5a7613c931d45d057eaca7b5ec15280aca76c9e` found source-scope, component-provenance and completeness defects that must be resolved before campaign integration. The review covers all188 cases and100 selected payloads with three separate scientific reviewers and an independent final assembly review. It grants no owner, role or export approval.\n\nThe current ordinary successor is `1b3641853c7105b9091f81b5a9b19c99e8ed351e`, verified live. It addresses the known duplicate stock under #1207 and reports a separate Merck component-label correction. Re-review those exact successor bytes before retiring their findings. The remaining findings below need an immutable successor preserving published captures, payloads and native reviews.\n\n| Finding | Defect | Required bounded outcome |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| W06-IR-002 | Contextual numbered pointers and generic labels resolve globally | Preserve each exact non-identifying label and provenance as REJECTED_LABEL; qualify preferred/ontology labels for JCM151/187/284 and R-P-MODIFIED-VITAMINS (JCM1158); retain explicit occurrence routing. Do not reject established named stocks or source-qualified names merely because they contain a number or see-below text. |\n| W06-IR-003 | Merck108339 glucose component fails native reference-label validation | Use active component_name D-glucose for CHEBI:17634, preserve supplier spelling D(+)Glucose in assertion evidence, and rerun partonomy/exact-byte review. |\n| W06-IR-004 | JCM977 stock Water is asserted as literal source input | Remove Water from literal transcription or explicitly represent and evidence the aqueous-solvent inference using method CURATED_INTERPRETATION and truthful curator/LLM attribution. Preserve unknown solvent detail, stock volume and glucose form; basal790mL water is not stock water. |\n| W06-IR-005 | Acknowledged Water inferences use literal-transcription assertion method | Distinguish source-transcribed solute/concentration from inferred solvent. Use CURATED_INTERPRETATION with precisely attributed inference evidence and LLM provenance if retained, or omit untranscribed Water. MANUAL_CURATION requires actual human-supplied evidence and is not prescribed automatically. |\n| W06-IR-006 | Positive JCM381-to379 evidence is misclassified as failed search | Bind A-E-CAPTURE-121 to the successful exact primary381 body with original timestamp/hash, retain381→379 context and index provenance, then refresh evidence bindings. D-glucose identity needs no correction. |\n| W06-IR-007 | Bounded authorized product/stock curation is deferred as missing science | Provide bounded source/manufacturer-qualified proposals retaining UNKNOWN excipients/lot/SKU/doses/forms and explicit source discrepancies. EBIOS must remain tablets; TypeB must remain distinct from TypeA/pure casein; C.difficile BHI branch is Oxoid and must not inherit current SR0096E doses; RM may transcribe narrative molybdate while documenting parsed-table omission, unknown acid strength and solvent/final-volume details. Do not clear source/owner/export holds. |\n| W06-IR-008 | Four failed receiving pages are classified as positive primary evidence | Relabel the four empty responses as unsuccessful_search, preserve original captures/access times, and enumerate receiving occurrences lacking an applicable recovered primary page. Preserve valid197 formulation/support and source-dose holds. Recover exact alternatives only if needed; do not use primary metadata as proof. |\n| W06-IR-009 | TSY broth reasoning misstates frozen units | Correct the reasoning to the actual1000 ML_PER_L frozen value; retain the genuine unknown whole-broth formulation and do not infer constituents from its name. |\n| W06-IR-010 | MediaDive1886 lacks a source bridge to JCM187 | Hold this KG source applicability unresolved; require an exact original collection/medium/recipe occurrence linking compound1886 toJCM187. Preserve independently supported CultureMech JCM187 contexts and their component evidence; remove or qualify unsupported KG backlink until then. |\n| W06-IR-011 | YNB J240 quantity is misstated | Correct only J240 occurrence quantity in reasoning/evidence summaries to1g; keep exactSKU/grade unresolved. |\n| W06-IR-012 | N-Z-Amine requirement overlooks known Sheffield typeA contexts | State known SheffieldtypeA subset explicitly and identify remaining uncertainty as catalogue/historical composition and unspecified other occurrences. Either perform authorized bounded source-qualified curation/review for that subset or mark that as deferred authorized curation; do not label already captured supplier/grade facts unavailable. Do not inferSigmaC7290 or universalN-Z-Amine equivalence. |\n\nPrimary examples: [JCM977](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=977) names20%w/v glucose without an explicit stock-solvent preparation; its790mL distilled water belongs to the basal medium. [JCM381](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=381) successfully links379; its original body must not be labelled a failed search. Failed receiving-page captures for JCM737/876/887/955 contain only “Nothing found”; the valid JCM197 formulation remains separate. [JCM969](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=969) and captured TOGO M3181/M2811/M2815 supply bounded product or stock facts while historical formulation details remain unknown.\n\nThe frozen TSY quantity is1000ML_PER_L, and the exact MediaDive J240 YNB occurrence is1g. The other inspected YNB recipes use6.7g. Captured compound1608 receiving contexts already identify Sheffield typeA; this does not establish SigmaC7290 or universal N-Z-Amine equivalence. A providerless “see Medium No.” pointer needs an actual collection/recipe bridge, not a matching number alone.\n\nPreserve raw labels as provenance; retire resolving entries only where claim-specific evidence supports their non-identifying role. If a solvent inference is retained, use truthful CURATED_INTERPRETATION and actual LLM attribution, not fabricated human curation or literal recipe transcription. Keep genuine salt/form/SKU/dose/titrant/final-volume uncertainties and all88 downstream holds. Complete bounded authorized curation where evidence already settles its scope; do not force unresolved identities or collapse preparation differences.\n\nEvidence: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/workers/w03/worktree/.temp/w06-published-head-independent-review-v1/`. Findings SHA256 `4626520a16f0b5e3729f6ffc630fba623e579742b3361cd68667de9c2598dd27`; assessment `ea688186e9507893bf98720bcaeaf3f86112600c18a390b411499db9c06c0a9c`; complete manifest `ee57931deef8638f9cb13a4f8bbc657bf5a1ef938eeb7e0a173775a2e8135a66`. The coordinator verified all5038 manifest files and read the exact grouped findings, reproductions and bounded fixes. The source evidence/case IDs/affected payload digests are enumerated in that ledger and must accompany the published successor.\n\nLive all-state deduplication inspected675 issues and a fresh exact W06-IR search. #1207 remains the duplicate-stock tracker; #1201 is related completeness work, not a replacement for these named findings. Require per-finding dispositions, guarded isolated payload checks, complete case/occurrence accounting, native schema/partonomy and fresh independent final-head review. No maintained application, gate weakening, merge or downstream rebuild is authorized by this issue.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1217/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1217/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6268732544,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdaVEgA","number":1237,"title":"Reconcile source-bound preparation families before installing duplicate or unsupported owners","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":23,"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:30:15Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T11:53:11Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The completed independent preparation-comparison packets identify duplicate proposed preparations, source-continuity conflicts and unsupported claims of disjointness. This issue tracks only the bounded family decisions below. These are isolated proposals; no record merge, new namespace, scientific approval or export release is authorized by the review.\n\nAll three sealed packets were independently hash-checked: Worker01 878 files, Worker05 390, Worker10 526, with no hash mismatch or unlisted file in the ignored-inclusive inventories. Their assignments partition the 67 mechanical family leads (26/22/19); this means comparison coverage, not 67 resolved or approved identities. The exact 28 retained finding/obligation IDs are reduced to 26 rows in `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/family-findings-triage-v1/findings-matrix-v2.json`. Original authors, skeptical reviews, proposal bytes, primary capture times/hashes, source cases and occurrences remain immutable.\n\nA source accession, filename, receiving dose, missing carrier, unknown pH or unspecified hydrate does not prove a distinct supplied preparation. Nor does it prove equality. Source-qualified partial proposals remain useful; overlapping candidates need a defined scope or the missing evidence before simultaneous installation. No unknown is filled by guessing. Source-batch water and final-volume instructions remain separate, and immediate-list completeness is independent of molecular grounding.\n\n| Findings / frozen entries | Sourced conclusion and bounded next action |\n|---|---|\n| W01-FPC-PA-001 + MIN-F03; 573/810, maintained ATCC_Wolfes_Vitamin_Mix | JCM197, NBRC837 and NBRC903 give the same ten nominal vitamins and amounts plus1L water. Prepare one combined nominal candidate preserving all source-specific processing. The maintained ATCC owner has authentic branded MD-VS history and a D-(+) calcium-pantothenate specification; JCM/NBRC only say calcium pantothenate. Preserve that distinction in what the evidence asserts: unspecified stereo proves neither sameness nor difference. Do not automatically reuse ATCC or install two source-number owners. Establish the applicability bridge or explicitly decide nominal-recipe versus supplied-product scope before co-installation. |\n| MIN-F01; 624/657 | DSM590/1144 Hutner tables and preparation match at nominal scope. Preserve CaCl2·2H2O3.335g versus3.34g rounding and both malformed molybdate strings as literal unresolved assertions; do not turn a typographical discrepancy into a different chemical. Prepare one source-union nominal recipe candidate. Both underlying Metals44 instructions are retained; the current automatically extracted portal is not a historical erratum. |\n| MIN-F02, W05-CR-F02; 381–384/624/657/705 | Wolfe JCM470/DSM792, modified Wolfe ATCC1190/1191 versus JCM221, and Hutner JCM900/979 comparisons have explicit unresolved hydrate/reagent or preparation details. Correct claims that missing qualifiers prove incompatibility. Do not infer JCM470's variable Mn hydrate as monohydrate, or transfer ATCC final-volume/form-specific instructions to JCM221. Preserve the positively different JCM149 MgSO4 quantity14.45g versus29.7g. |\n| W01-FPC-PA-003; 747 plus existing JCM403 B12 owner | NBRC1321 explicitly gives cyanocobalamin5mg with100ml water; JCM403 specifies generic B12 at matching nominal quantities. Preserve both levels of specificity. Missing JCM vitamer/preparation evidence is an unresolved relation, not a proved difference or an exact identity bridge. Coordinate the existing JCM403 promotion/pointer correction under1201/1227; do not create a competing owner by accession alone. |\n| W01-PREP-B-001; 619 | NBRC1507 names0.1M Tris/HCl pH7.5 stock but does not list free hydrochloric acid as a separate component. Remove that unsupported free-acid has-part claim. Preserve the literal named buffer, strength and pH with unknown complete composition; do not substitute dry Tris-HCl salt or invent solvent/neutralization. |\n| W01-PREP-B-002 + CHEM-COMP-003; 669 | JCM1479 positively specifies a5% L-cysteine-HCl-monohydrate stock atpH7. Unreported pH of other5% stocks does not establish a different substance. Correct the comparison wording, retain stock/solid separation and the unknown percentage basis/carrier/titrant. |\n| CHEM-COMP-002; 6/13 | NBRC1020 prints Na2WO4; JCM317 explicitly prints dihydrate, both at4mg with4mg selenite and1L water. Remove the claim that omission proves anhydrous NBRC1020 or disjointness. Preserve both literal tables and ask only for the missing supplied form if full chemical equivalence is needed. |\n| CHEM-COMP-004; 943/944/946/106 | Literal35%,32%,25% HCl and qualitative concentrated labels have unknown comparable bases; M2305/M2746 even call their25% input concentrated. Correct categorical disjointness without converting percentages or inventing a carrier. Retain source qualification; an explicit common partial-material scope or comparable formulation evidence is needed before consolidation. |\n| BIO-COMP-005; 328/333 with283/287/288/290 | Historical MJ and JCM1216 0.1x artificial-seawater formulations remain partly unspecified. Missing recipe/version is not evidence of a different formulation. Preserve the source-qualified preparations, positive known differences and exact missing historical MJ/1x-base specification; no guessed formula or wholesale seawater merge. |\n| BIO-COMP-001; 201/476 | CM0643 prepared broth and dry powder are different supplied forms. The source handles for entry201 use1000ml/10ml broth; entry476 weighs33g powder. Correct entry201's dry-powder representation and account for its authentic existing broth provenance. Retain powder separate from prepared broth, water and receiving supplements; the same catalogue does not erase the supplied-form boundary. MICRO:0002186 describes liquid, so any use requires whole-broth§3 scope review and must not identify powder. |\n| BIO-F02; 971 + Swine_Serum | The new DSM1076b heat-inactivated swine-serum proposal uses MediaDive960, already the creation source of Swine_Serum/UNMAPPED_0536. Reconcile or promote through that authentic preimage/history. Do not add a second same-source owner or label the separate generic Porcine_Serum/MD967 untreated. Heat schedule remains unknown. |\n| BIO-F03; 970 + Bovine_Calf_Serum | JCM1303 heat-inactivated calf serum uses MediaDive2061, already the import source of Bovine_Calf_Serum. Audit its broader/Gibco occurrences and partition their applicability before narrowing or adding an owner. Missing historical heat metadata is not an untreated claim. No wholesale repurposing or maintained-owner merge. |\n| BIO-F04; 893/908/914/916/922 | Withdraw unsupported serum exclusions: bovine does not exclude fetal; gamma irradiation does not exclude heat treatment; unspecified heat schedule need not differ from a specified one. Retain positive age/species/catalogue/process facts and actual30/45/60minute or active/inactivated differences. No forced product equivalence. |\n| BIO-F05; 904/906 | JCM946 supports56C30min heating and filtration before addition, but not their relative order. Clarify only that ordering claim. DSM1021 explicitly requires sterile fetal/newborn alternatives; preserve sterility for the selected newborn scope without inventing heat or filter treatment. |\n| BIO-F06; 300/921 | Oxoid CM0331 and TOGO M2224 disclose the same nominal dry base: special peptone23g, starch1g, NaCl5g, agar10g, pH7.3±0.2. Prepare one combined formulation candidate while retaining which source actually states the catalogue. Before installation, account for existing Columbia_Blood_Agar_Base's mixed Oxoid/Difco provenance; do not repurpose the entire owner. Preserve the distinct Difco/BBL/EH formulations. Blood and reconstitution water are not dry-base parts. |\n| BIO-F07; 980 | Replace a search-wrapper-as-primary assertion with the recovered2009 BD manufacturer manual capture, p158. Keep original wrapper, older manual edition and failed URLs as historical evidence. This verifies the nominal Difco formulation, not a historical lot or arbitrary vendor equivalence. |\n| BIO-F08; 919 | Current ATCC0988 is explicitly reformulated asMD2611 and specifies ATCC30-2020 plus55C treatment; frozen TOGO M2578 preserves older fetal/newborn alternatives and unknown schedule. Keep both versions and their exact applicability. Same URL is not same document; this is a version obligation, not a finding that the frozen transcription is false. |\n| CHEM-COMP-006; 35/36 | Reassess new claim-specific resolver dispositions. The fully specified0.01M FeSO4·7H2O in0.02N HCl name is not shown to be a non-name merely because a global alias was undesirable. Bicarbonate footnote pointers have different ambiguity. Preserve all existing rejected entries; do not blanket-reactivate or blanket-reject authentic labels. Under§3, any new rejection needs claim-specific evidence; owned-name suppression applies only when its ownership condition holds. Historical1173 lineage is not a new scientific decision. |\n\nAdditional reconciliation groups with positive evidence can proceed to isolated candidate preparation, with exact-byte independent review before application:\n\n- DAIGO395-01681 entries188/474: one named dry product, eight manufacturer components. Preserve the manufacturer/JCM peptone wording and exact hydrate, the3.15g listed sum versus3.2g preparation instruction, and both histories. Do not invent another constituent, agar, water, generic DSM1537 applicability or wholesale KG1402 routing. The local identifier is already shared; choose one readable destination by the product scope, not author order.\n- Mixed phosphate entries873/940: one nominal preparation from equal volumes of1M KH2PO4 and1M Na2HPO4. Preserve50+50ml versus10+10ml batches and PBBM-onlypH7.2. The immediate input list can be complete without claiming its input stocks' exact hydrate, solvent or neutralization chemistry.\n- HEPES-KOH1M entries449/450 (W05-CR-F01): both sources positively name the same nominal strength/neutralizer; receiving-mediumpH7.14/9.0 is not stockpH. Recommend an explicit common bounded nominal scope if that is the intended owner model; otherwise retain candidate holds for actual stockpH/carrier/neutralization evidence. Do not install two proved-distinct preparations based solely on source numbers.\n- 95% ethanol entries460–463 (W05-CR-F03): preserve proven within-protocol reuse and every occurrence. A shared bounded partial-material scope is an option, but neither four distinct complete formulations nor equality follows without percentage basis/carrier/denaturant/product evidence. Do not infer95%v/v aqueous NCIT identity. Missing composition is not permission to discard the supported partial material.\n\nExisting trackers are reused, not duplicated:1206 JCM852;1210 sodium-thiosulfate tetrahydrate;1202 Polypeptone;1212 Phytone/SoyPeptone;1217 W06 source/solvent provenance;1221 EBIOS;1204 rumen. For rumen the current sourced decision explicitly leaves the three dependent parents' literal rumen-fluid components UNMAPPED; the older comparison suggestion to redirect them to clarified fluid is superseded, not fresh evidence. The Tris-HCl parent-grade defect is filed separately because its exact record correction/native repro is distinct from these formulation decisions.\n\nPrimary source anchors: [JCM197](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=197), [NBRC903](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=903), [ATCC2672](https://www.atcc.org/-/media/product-assets/documents/microbial-media-formulations/2/6/7/2/atcc-medium-2672.pdf?rev=7f27672230474579b9151e4c2ec9f20a), [DSM590](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium590.pdf), [DSM1144](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1144.pdf), [JCM470](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=470), [NBRC1507](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1507), [DSM1076b](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1076b.pdf), [JCM1303](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1303), [Oxoid CM0331 specification](https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/MBD/Specification-Sheets/PS-CM0331-V6.pdf), [TOGO M2224](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M2224), [BD2009 manual](https://fsl.nmsu.edu/documents/difcobblmanual_2nded_lowres.pdf), [DAIGO manufacturer](https://labchem-wako.fujifilm.com/jp/product/detail/W01N0139-0168.html). Every capture's exact original URL/time/hash and case binding is retained in the triage indexes and source packets; links alone are not treated as immutable evidence.\n\nDo not apply the original frozen W06 payloads just because their historical paths still exist. Six selected W06 payloads and its new EBIOS proposal have advanced and need exact successor comparisons. W07's observed successor was metadata-only in the source comparison, but its actual selected bytes still require final intake readback. All source, role and release holds remain content-bound.\n\nExact frozen source origins retained for these findings (later successors require explicit bridges):\n\n| Entry | Original proposal | Source head | Exact payload SHA256 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 6 | `w01::NSV4-PROP-NBRC_1020_Se_W_Solution` | `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c` | `235072e64c69a7dc51f9386f0664d69ffab234a5a0cca427cf4b4b18b37de0e7` |\n| 13 | `w01::NSV4-PROP-JCM_317_Se_W_Solution` | `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c` | `1603001c438fc6e321f1f105cff5ebd5a9f2be169e5657493de1d8b49a4ace62` |\n| 35 | `w01::CS-PROP-JCM1430_FERROUS_SULFATE_HCL_STOCK` | `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c` | `6e0ae3d8ec0984d7e29034b2fd41d3589f26fb7f236bdcc7a829d632837e0c59` |\n| 36 | `w01::CS-PROP-NBRC1321_CO2_BICARBONATE_STOCK` | `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c` | `61c0a226a8a99d96b43657f6e00075e901ce051a698b01bd99f6ab6f1d88717c` |\n| 106 | `w02::a2-proposal-togo-m2746-m2305-hydrochloric-acid-25percent` | `0597d00417be4d7cdfb5a31970043eec9bbc88fe` | `70c016d0e74a8487668258f66ab8ae63722e4ecbf6cce3b4c7890caaa9054a51` |\n| 188 | `w03::b-proposal-daigo-r2a` | `1196d5bc3aaba7563b829d5cbe7e54722fccc35d` | `5603b8878ca3460906dcc26b33c29db602661773eb3a598ad293ae7cd525b22f` |\n| 201 | `w03::b-proposal-cm0643` | `1196d5bc3aaba7563b829d5cbe7e54722fccc35d` | `1646156e0153d035e585214dd25eaa6275a423bc41920aa34cc68a02992aa4e6` |\n| 283 | `w04::BIO-PROPOSAL-jcm_492_modified_mj_synthetic_seawater` | `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9` | `ddd35feefd2df9b1f2a3d721f5b3d89926988efc6e7210a1269e243d324d8f16` |\n| 287 | `w04::BIO-PROPOSAL-jcm_651_artificial_seawater_05x` | `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9` | `0adde845da6ee89a25d28a821e889727dd5136c6ae3015c4e6eb17781dc9095a` |\n| 288 | `w04::BIO-PROPOSAL-jcm_910_artificial_seawater_1x` | `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9` | `4557113d7ff49fdd8722ba409e1d5e1016d44b5f51f528a644c0048d9eeaa107` |\n| 290 | `w04::BIO-PROPOSAL-jcm_1269_artificial_seawater_4x` | `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9` | `71008fd600cde88d17a6315c0147b00ca48890df2cb53ce643c794853640899c` |\n| 300 | `w04::media-followup-oxoid_cm0331_columbia_blood_agar_base` | `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9` | `560e2e3301550c952b729956e1a04c87941304888130adbe52a254e747207e69` |\n| 328 | `w04::I1201-BIO-P-m3127_mj_synthetic_seawater` | `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9` | `fcf44fd32461fdd13b84b33eed72aee991591f78cdbde06433389d0ea104e7a1` |\n| 333 | `w04::I1201-BIO-P-jcm1216_artificial_seawater_01x` | `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9` | `227335e425995406a3e50df0ea4fe1a897a429756bd16acdee59057059a37104` |\n| 381 | `w05::R1193-P-wolfe470` | `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` | `59fdf6607b5ae8add60ff70972c6b2ac143e7fe0d5212b50896cb886315c2069` |\n| 382 | `w05::R1193-P-wolfe1190` | `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` | `8efc7361c2a14db7279703d3c824b7b43c36afdb8fbfe6ec0972e52d7405eade` |\n| 383 | `w05::R1193-P-wolfe221` | `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` | `ce7ea091fa3d6d935e7020dea064033aee56cbaee90603adab3e624ccbe7fb77` |\n| 384 | `w05::R1193-P-wolfe792` | `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` | `b8ccaea9515441fbee3edb15d5edf3951f2c4729278a82e3219ae751890e5ea4` |\n| 449 | `w05::CHEM-C1193-HEPES-1221` | `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` | `05cf4a1b09aff0fd1954ef0ac1aa563844414f4896261eaca48271323d9f8a46` |\n| 450 | `w05::CHEM-C1193-HEPES-1474` | `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` | `6ba28f7de8b9b6387fb38f44ec01ce9b9626a84bea256ea63b7d0df07b109fad` |\n| 460 | `w05::CHEM-C1193-ethanol95-atcc_1490` | `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` | `84691f529ce8d1e146d2dc2c37b1ecc87027e2cf52ccd60007d6908d8bb5fe14` |\n| 461 | `w05::CHEM-C1193-ethanol95-atcc_1257` | `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` | `fa52d73955f5d54be470eaa21c1de4ef59eda6b6fe95431d6a37cf9782975365` |\n| 462 | `w05::CHEM-C1193-ethanol95-atcc_1524` | `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` | `3da7ef96a6d1020c39ca9663c045a913acc0b68cc060b674304399fe62f576cc` |\n| 463 | `w05::CHEM-C1193-ethanol95-dsmz_78` | `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` | `5718e7de2922144c0e8b8bc519b6fddb637989975d99f0d7737dc4335ac96a9d` |\n| 474 | `w05::M1193-P-R2A-DAIGO` | `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` | `82a75f1ba268a903d32a8b62b2b8ee918ad6ac2ba7591b084f99a27702bd4dc7` |\n| 476 | `w05::M1193-P-CM0643` | `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` | `4c9ad4e62517234ca0cb7b4c58f6dbd33f4fe8319a2f1ba36d9e7752f05fc9b0` |\n| 573 | `w06::C-P-JCM197` | `1b3641853c7105b9091f81b5a9b19c99e8ed351e` | `de17dee3c912e05f2ac460ef85d296a8f6d0a20a175de173233a41cb522b8063` |\n| 619 | `w07::A-PROPOSAL-NBRC1507_Tris_HCl_01M_pH75_Buffer` | `fbfa032435ea1c399ae9b98bfedadb9ed639430d` | `fee1ee6d50153341ac16a466551a95edcf47ad2b3a532a72e283a7205837bbdd` |\n| 624 | `w07::A-PROPOSAL-DSM590_Hutner_Basal_Salts` | `fbfa032435ea1c399ae9b98bfedadb9ed639430d` | `51024df2e489d3a58ad0ed9d6d1fbe3f0928d64610edb295b03b4e25e5dc9f27` |\n| 657 | `w07::B-PROPOSAL-dsmz_1144_hutner_basal_salts` | `fbfa032435ea1c399ae9b98bfedadb9ed639430d` | `53c