8` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `e095ee1af7fe44564fb8ad4bda0620a68beab2201749e5d95377fc90a32d7273` |\n| 921 | `w10::sv1-bio-columbia_blood_agar_oxoid_m2224` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `814a2a4b8c196b50f0d14b6280f79c6ee3cdcb9372a15469fb8fa58d96fdf639` |\n| 922 | `w10::sv1-bio-fetal_bovine_serum_56c_60min_m2964` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `3d85af4e8d854ce3f5c6a5a5588de2d1a788d00aa97a732a5711c0670f61a58b` |\n| 940 | `w10::sv1-buffers-phosphate_1m_ph7_2_pbbm_togo_m2760` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `092dc9e4f5e24d02ade620ba3346988b7d4466501a779a2a11867512b99f7a61` |\n| 943 | `w10::sv1-buffers-hcl_nominal35percent_togo_m3216` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `e7feec90fa5d94bc8a3003be08b94de71b9119a528787eb68784b3c5413ab55c` |\n| 944 | `w10::sv1-buffers-hcl_nominal32percent_jcm770` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `4ca8faefe79f29c649c1e1b82468314bd454abd0abd41d732fe09b7b54ce17eb` |\n| 946 | `w10::sv1-buffers-hcl_nominal25percent_jcm431_899` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `74e1276709349d844cc7c883b3d3554f8e8fce876d8798ef930f3e955c40b02c` |\n| 970 | `w10::sv1-kg-calf-serum1303` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `c5095e48aa60fc9dde875bc49e1d1628f9869ab53d606ca10c42622de9b77a78` |\n| 971 | `w10::sv1-kg-swine-serum1076b` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `855514ece2c881918f44112a0f3c52cb855b0e05642cf5af267235a1936a10c7` |\n| 980 | `w10::sv1-kg-difco-columbia1270` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `07b3aa3689dbee44e18c5c4d416ebee0ba5920a5eb044cd7901cda9d7f8ab0e7` |\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/811","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/811/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/811/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/811/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/811","id":5707496789,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABVDF9VQ","number":811,"title":"Label-index answers still wrong or missing for CultureMech recipe labels (pin-refresh replay)","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-05T06:32:57Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T07:13:29Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Source\n\nFound while refreshing CultureMech's vendored MIM label index to `6643131b`. I replayed every recipe label in CultureMech's occurrence table through the old and new pins; the method is from CultureBotAI/CultureMech#417. The pin refresh is a large improvement overall (99% of rows unchanged, and the changes are mostly hydrate-specific corrections). These are the labels where MIM's **current** answer still looks wrong or missing. In each case the old answer was no better, so none of this blocks the pin.\n\n## Wrong form\n\n| CultureMech label | recipe rows | resolves to | problem |\n|---|---:|---|---|\n| `MnSO4・xH2O` (+ `MnSO4·nH2O`) | 61 | CHEBI:86364, `MnSO4 x 1 H2O` | A variable hydrate resolves to the monohydrate. The variable-sulfate precedent (#646 and others) gives these a local `x n H2O` identity. |\n| `NiCl2 x H2O`, `NiCl2・H2O` | ~5 | CHEBI:53542, nickel(II) chloride hexahydrate | A monohydrate label resolves to the hexahydrate. |\n| `Trisodium citrate x 3 H2O` | 2 | CHEBI:53258 | A trihydrate label resolves to a non-trihydrate term. |\n| `Potassium phosphate` | 4 | CHEBI:63036 | A generic label resolves to one specific potassium phosphate salt. |\n\nThe NaH2PO4 monohydrate spellings that resolve to the dihydrate record (~36 rows) are already tracked as #758.\n\n## Missing or ambiguous\n\n- **`sodium nitrate`, 58 rows, unresolved:** ambiguous because the stock-solution record `Sodium nitrate (0.70 M stock)` (`kgmicrobe.ingredient:sodium_nitrate_~28070_m_stock~29`) carries the bare compound name as a synonym next to CHEBI:63005. A stock solution's record shouldn't claim the compound's name.\n- **`α-Ketoglutarate`, 3 rows, now unresolved:** #232 correctly retired it from the disodium-salt record as `REJECTED_LABEL`, but no record now claims the anion or acid name.\n- **`Sea Salt`, now unindexed:** the old pin had it ambiguous through two `ontology_label` rows. Either way it got no identity, but no record claims generic sea salt.\n\nThe full replay table is in the CultureMech pin-refresh PR description.\n\n## More from the CultureMech#537 review (same replay)\n\n- **`MgSO4 x H2O` (12 rows) and `MgSO4 . H2O` (1) → CHEBI:31795, magnesium sulfate *heptahydrate*.** These resolve as trusted `mim_exact` through a REJECTED tombstone row on `Mgso47h2o.yaml` that carries the monohydrate label. Under the old pin they were flagged ambiguous; now they're confidently wrong, and KGX emits the edge.\n- **`Na2MoO4.H2O`, `Na2MoO4 . H2O`, `Na2MoO4 · H2O` (3 rows) → CHEBI:75213, the *dihydrate*,** by the same tombstone-row pattern.\n- **`sodium glutarate` (1 row): a regression.** It used to resolve to `cas:13521-83-0` (disodium glutarate). MIM no longer indexes that `ontology_label`, so CultureMech falls back to the recipe's local CHEBI:24329, the glutarate anion: a salt collapsed onto its parent.\n- **NaH2PO4 monohydrate spellings split:** `NaH2PO4•H2O` → CHEBI:114249 (the monohydrate), while `NaH2PO4 x H2O` / `·H2O` go to the dihydrate record (#758). Two spellings of one substance get different identities.\n\nRoot pattern for the first two: merge tombstones keep raw labels naming a *different hydrate* than their survivor, and the label index publishes them as REJECTED rows that consumers follow by contract.\n\n## From the unified-mapping fix (culturebotai-claw#571)\n\n- **`MgSO .7H O` (17 occurrences)** is a safe (`unique`) synonym on the *anhydrous* Magnesium sulfate record (CHEBI:32599), but it's a garbled heptahydrate label. Its recipes carry the correct heptahydrate CHEBI:31795. Now that the unified mapping follows MIM's label index, this MIM synonym placement decides the published identity.\n- **`Na2HPO4·7H2O`** has no label-index row; only other spellings of the heptahydrate are indexed. So its recipes' anhydrous CHEBI:34683 still wins (MIM#808).\n\n## From the claw#571 review: MIM record and synonym defects that now decide unified-mapping identities\n\n| label (occurrences) | MIM's `unique` answer | problem |\n|---|---|---|\n| `DL-Tryptophan` (4) | record `DL-Tryptophan` on CHEBI:57912 | CHEBI:57912 is the L-tryptophan zwitterion, so the racemate is recorded as an enantiomer |\n| `Na2-DL-malate`, `Sodium DL-malate`, `Na-DL-malate` and others (26) | `Sodium malate`, CHEBI:91261 | DL labels sit on a disodium (S)-malate identity |\n| `Na2SiO3` (8) | synonym on `Na2SiO3 x 9 H2O` (CHEBI:132108) | an anhydrous formula label on the nonahydrate |\n| `Magnesium Chloride` (5) | record `Magnesium chloride` = CHEBI:86345 | a generic name owns the hexahydrate identity |\n| `MgSO .7H O` (17) | synonym on anhydrous `Magnesium sulfate` | a garbled heptahydrate label (noted above) |\n\n## From the second claw#571 review\n\n- **Sodium malate family** (`Sodium malate` 14, `Sodium DL-malate` 11, `Na2-DL-malate` 6, `Na-malate` 6, `Na malate` 4, `Na-DL-malate` 4, `DL-Na-malate` 3, `DL-Sodium malate` 2; 50 occurrences): MIM's `Sodium malate` record sits on CHEBI:91261, disodium **(S)**-malate, while the labels are racemic or stereo-unspecified. The recipes carry CHEBI:91260 (disodium malate).\n- **`H3BO2`** (3): an unreviewed import record grounds this (likely a typo for H3BO3, boric acid) to boronic acid CHEBI:38267.\n\n\n## Update 2026-10-14 (second review of #881)\n\n**Fixed in #881:**\n- `MgSO4 x H2O`, `MgSO4 . H2O` and `MgSO4・H2O` now resolve to the monohydrate `cas:14168-73-1` (#893).\n- `MgSO .7H O` now resolves to the heptahydrate CHEBI:31795 (#899).\n\n**Still open, same class, from the label index on #881's head:**\n\nDamaged-subscript formula labels resolving to the anhydrous form or to a different compound:\n\n| label | `label_index.csv` answer | CultureMech recipe rows |\n|---|---|---:|\n| `CaCl .6H O` | CHEBI:3312, anhydrous CaCl2 | 5 |\n| `ZnCl .6H O` | CHEBI:49976, anhydrous ZnCl2 | 3 |\n| `EDTA.Na .2H O` | CHEBI:64734 (`Na2-EDTA`) | 3 |\n| `CoCl .6H O` | CHEBI:35696, anhydrous CoCl2 | 0 |\n| `FeSO .7H O` | CHEBI:75832, anhydrous FeSO4 | 0 |\n| `LiCl.H O` | CHEBI:48607, anhydrous LiCl | 0 |\n| `NaH PO .2H O` | CHEBI:37585, anhydrous NaH2PO4 | 0 |\n| `ZnSO .7H O` | CHEBI:86463 (`AlK(SO4)2`), a different compound | 0 |\n| `Na SiO .9H O` | CHEBI:86463 (`AlK(SO4)2`), a different compound | 0 |\n\nWater-ratio names resolving to a different hydrate:\n- `cobalt(2+) sulfate--water (1/7)` → CHEBI:53470, anhydrous CoSO4;\n- `Cobalt(II) chloride--water (1/7)` → CHEBI:53503, the hexahydrate.\n\n**Consistency question, not an explicit contradiction:** `Mgso4_X_7_H2o` carries four names, all ChEBI related synonyms of CHEBI:32599:\n- `magnesium sulphate`;\n- `magnesium(II) sulfate`;\n- `sulfuric acid magnesium salt`;\n- `sulphate of magnesia`.\n\nThey resolve to the heptahydrate, while `Magnesium sulfate` resolves to the anhydrous form. Semantic-review finding SEM:f345b845583ac48792ef is open on this.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/811/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/811/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1259","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1259/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1259/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1259/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1259","id":6271154579,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdco5kw","number":1259,"title":"Add a guarded campaign transition for independently reviewed suppression events","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-11-08T12:57:38Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T13:54:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The current campaign publisher correctly refuses four new selected owned-name suppression events, but has no closed route to consume their independent review and preserve historical sidecar provenance. This is a bounded #1174 capability extension under #669, separate from #1150's older companion-history compatibility defect.\n\nThe exact conditional W07 review covers Bacto_Peptone/peptone, Glebomycin/bluensomycin, Netropsin/congocidin and Starch/corn starch, with complete credited-owner sets and eight whole owners. It does not authorize application, whole-owner acceptance or mapping/role/export admission. Congocidin's unresolved placeholder and other scientific holds remain. All four event keys are new to the historical sidecar; only Corn Starch is presently in an old canonical `other` field, so do not describe this as four old-token removals.\n\nProvide a narrow versioned campaign publication transition that consumes an exact independently reviewed decision binding to actual source completion, current complete owner inventory, native generation and each full event/credit tuple. Preserve the 34 historical sidecar rows physically and append only the four actual reviewed native events. Preserve the baseline, historical 2,955-owner attribution, all prior policy histories and native receipts 1–27; bind the new transition in one approval-free native campaign successor. Do not reuse historical 11/23-pair pins, replace the sidecar with the 21-event diagnostic, change owner-selection rules or bypass Rule K.\n\nExtend existing output reservation, guards, expected-byte recovery backups, late checks and independent replay to the third sidecar target. Test genuine source→native generation→publication, exact positive history retention, full credit sets and all review/source/alias/late-drift/partial-completion negatives. Existing `_validate_pair` is reusable structural validation but cannot establish expected event completeness or credit correctness alone; those require the closed review/inventory contract. Diagnostic source paths and manifest hashes must be explicitly bridged to actual application evidence, not rewritten in prior reviews.\n\nTechnical proposal and actual structural controls: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/four-suppression-publication-design-v1`. No suppression implementation or corpus application has occurred in this packet. Root must select the final exact independent binding and review the implemented guard before use.\n\nDesign manifest SHA256 `439aabb5c3edcd9ae683a54f18db9a10ba5a7981b42d77f000f5104e2bedfb32`; root rehashed all18members. The genuine W07 conditional science review is sealed with manifest `96283373897369bdd1f010087442fefea84f574000a46e8314d678010c913076`, decision `26c5f381bcf3600f18c54722213c076389d0d17d732bbf760783e1cfdc4d333c`, and native review YAML `99bef708606134cf404608f52e4fa61696fb67412122a27ade5c789d345c1f71`; root rehashed all2,391members and50handoff references. It has15genuine owner captures plus the explicit Corn_Starch null preimage, not16existing owner files.\n\nIndependent design review is checking the actual review/peer scopes and proposed transaction. The current fixed registry-row publisher is PR1205 head `e0a75a0c48ba539426b1f70623ea376c7b379ecf`; this issue's suppression extension is still unimplemented. File this scope before code changes; validate and independently review the eventual exact producer head before any campaign application. Existing version1 plans must continue refusing new suppression events.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1259/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1259/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241","id":6268856056,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdacm-A","number":1241,"title":"Correct Worker02 source scope, quantity prose and review accounting before final acceptance","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:48:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T09:55:03Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Correct Worker02 source scope, quantity prose and review accounting before final acceptance\n\nReviewed W02 head `0597d00417be4d7cdfb5a31970043eec9bbc88fe`, frozen campaign base `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99`. Authoritative peer review is `assembly-v2/review.yaml` (SHA256 `31cac38cae0cfb3dcfae4453a01402dc98d249f70ad9a7698a89b25eed5eae11`) in the sealed W04 independent W02 packet, whose 2,399-member SHA256SUMS is `99306617655b1e3df84368079e49f4341a0fd05667bdf9fedf18dda24f4f7ca7`. The coordinator verified all manifest members, rebound all188 case decisions and106 selected payloads, and independently repeated all106 native guarded writes and baseline/overlay partonomy. Structural validation passes; the scientific verdict remains needs_curation. These are unapplied proposal corrections, not changes already made to main or whole-owner/export approval.\n\nThis tracker groups defects in the same published W02 source/proposal artifact. It does not reopen every historical owner review. Stable finding IDs and complete targets remain in the immutable native review.\n\n| Finding | Exact bounded correction |\n|---|---|\n| W02-F-QUANTITY / W02-RA-02 | Four selected preparation narratives: JCM167 requires water to a final900mL; TOGO M683/JCM665 requires make-up to1L. DSMZ40 C/D/E provider section volumes must not become measured whole-stock aliquots; the inherited DSMZ29 recipe distinguishes water additions and other stocks. MRSsi is expressed per litre, not proven1L of added water. Structured component concentrations were not found defective. Preserve earlier history and append corrections. |\n| W02-F-TYPE / W02C-001 | JCM378 nutrient basal preparation,50%v/v methanol, and0.025%resazurin are marked MINERAL_STOCK, whose schema meaning is concentrated mineral stock. Choose the justified existing category, including OTHER if necessary; no new role inference. |\n| W02-F-METHANOL-SOURCE / W02C-004 | TOGO M1257 is JCM1173-2, using GRMD1173, not1174. Correct the active preferred/mapping/source labels while preserving all six occurrences and the same supported50%v/v stock. |\n| W02-F-MN-SOURCE-CONFLICT / w02-external-b-005 | Case41's17-occurrence manganese applicability includes CM_OCC:9b15f04e391224356807bef1a5f82b76de2fbbcef5ef448cf468b6520d535c3b. The frozen provider entry says MnSO4·xH2O33.8mg/L, but the exact original JCM1503 first trace row says MgCl2·6H2O33.8mg. Partition this source-version/identity conflict from supported Mn occurrences. Nearby source typos do not establish which reagent is right; do not change frozen source bytes or globally assign Mg by guess. |\n| W02-F-FERRIC-AVAILABILITY / w02-external-b-006 | Case124's retained JCM413 and603 captures are successful recipe references to369 and592 with modifications. Correct claims of source unavailability, bind complete modification/base chains and retain genuinely missing reagent/form/quantity facts. Own-CAS and duplicate-owner decisions remain on873. |\n| W02-F-NICKEL-OWNER-BINDING / w02-external-b-008 | Case115 binds only REJECTED Niso4_X_6_H2o. Compare and bind the active Nickel_II_sulfate_hexahydrate owner; preserve the rejected record as history. Do not reactivate it, approve malformedNi2SO4 globally, or erase the historical EXCLUDED_REJECTED review. |\n| W02-F-EVIDENCE-CLASSIFICATION / W02-RA-01, w02-external-b-007, W02C-COVERAGE-001 | Nine actual Nothing-found responses are not positive recipe evidence: three are referenced by active cases2/30/152/184, JCM1250 also remains in the ferric proposal, five are historical unlinked evidence. Distinguish the failed CAS Common Chemistry detail response too. b2-chebi-30729 is valid ontology evidence, not original ammonium-reagent recipe evidence. Preserve original bytes/times; successful bacmedia recoveries are separate sources, not retrospective success. |\n| W02-F-PUBLICATION-LINEAGE / W02-ASSEMBLY-01 | Add an immutable author-published ledger covering all72 prior stable finding IDs and735 historical finding/reference objects, linking complete targets, exact old hashes, deduplicated issues, corrections, independent re-reviews and residual holds. A private external ledger or broad handoff link does not provide this author publication lineage. Do not blanket reopen/close corrected science. |\n\nPrimary checks: [JCM167](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=167); [TOGO M683](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M683); [TOGO M2491](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M2491); [TOGO M1257](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M1257); [JCM1503](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1503). The sealed exact captures and coordinator primary-finding-readback.json retain response hashes and original access times. JCM1503 SHA256 is `01c7a36ad95a0d476f5fc1806413145c63c56de7bf270d6fbdd006795c6800ef`.\n\n| Proposal | Owner | Exact selected SHA256 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `a-proposal-chrome-alum` | `data/ingredients/mapped/CrKSO42_X_12_H2O.yaml` | `e4f2fb4d6d39e19bdbad76bbd5a8cedbf960507fb825714922fb6a4d0d19c5d0` |\n| `a-proposal-strontium-sulfate` | `data/ingredients/mapped/Strontium_sulfate.yaml` | `ce0a68da191d5d3b0aa447b83d1d6aacb11594d7528e48f3210c39804c9fcfae` |\n| `a2-proposal-dsmz40-cde-mixed-preparation` | `data/ingredients/mapped/dsmz40_cde_mixed_preparation.yaml` | `1d4bb6decf8b68edebbdc1dabf670804624c20d01b0e59adb5bd0526d25cd97e` |\n| `a2-proposal-jcm167-precarbonate-basal-agar` | `data/ingredients/mapped/jcm167_precarbonate_basal_agar.yaml` | `4409f51db458621b0cb67ef34639fee49863bbf90e9ea8fd97ebda74267ebd5c` |\n| `a2-proposal-jcm378-preaddition-basal-preparation` | `data/ingredients/mapped/jcm378_preaddition_basal_preparation.yaml` | `6511f1be0d51490e09fb693ff8354d18a26c08d6eeccb7e7192dac894eb49844` |\n| `a2-proposal-jcm665-preaddition-iron-gel-base` | `data/ingredients/mapped/jcm665_preaddition_iron_gel_base.yaml` | `db1b027dde687f0afabdb0068f6aa0bce7006eb5f5206597581595ed92b96fb4` |\n| `a2-proposal-manganese-sulfate-variable-hydrate` | `data/ingredients/mapped/manganese_sulfate_variable_hydrate.yaml` | `ac7c4e146dd7b40fc76b77066c6e36e63e52394adaf98f81e4d1c8534bc838a3` |\n| `a2-proposal-togo-m2491-mrssi-base` | `data/ingredients/mapped/togo_m2491_mrssi_base.yaml` | `3838ea36856afdd637869e7818a855779a60d63067406ba08ede81bc80f045c4` |\n| `b2-proposal-Ferric_ammonium_EDTA` | `data/ingredients/mapped/Ferric_ammonium_EDTA.yaml` | `a34676d09ff73c29cbd8d6dd8db3d80723c459bbc392a747962c2651ad71abf5` |\n| `b2-proposal-methanol_50_percent_vv_jcm_sources` | `data/ingredients/mapped/methanol_50_percent_vv_jcm_sources.yaml` | `1e7ef83bf7afacdc950c4e2013a6ce1dc3550e503a1810780ebdd50ca27b0348` |\n| `b2-proposal-resazurin_0025_percent_atcc_chopped_meat` | `data/ingredients/mapped/resazurin_0025_percent_atcc_chopped_meat.yaml` | `43559067e33088d4353e4b9d37babf9996f6304afbcedbba1b15d0b77069d45a` |\n| `w02-v2-ferric-variable-composed` | `data/ingredients/mapped/Fe2_So43_X_N_H2o.yaml` | `ca1c64bdf0ab2178eb19f91ab46103783b39343787f5bdd151cb28f12b3fe20c` |\n\nDeduplication:1201 covers missing feasible curation, not these incorrect active quantity/category/source and publication fields.1173 and1223 track other workers' publication lineage.873 owns ferric identity/alias competition and receives the exact companion comment. Live all-state source/name and comment searches found no exact dedicated W02 tracker for this set; this does not assert that every historical GitHub comment is indexed.\n\nPreserve published original payloads/reviews, capture timestamps, histories, rejected text and all precise source/form/role/release holds. Prepare immutable corrected proposals through existing guarded validation, record claim-specific changes, and obtain independent review of the exact successor. No corpus application, owner merge, gate/schema/test/producer change or approval transfer follows from this issue.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1117","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1117/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1117/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1117/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1117","id":6173685176,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABb_r1uA","number":1117,"title":"Evaluate exact NCIt identities for sodium carbonate and D-maltose monohydrate","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T00:31:28Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T04:20:40Z","closed_at":"2026-11-04T04:20:40Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The Step 7d preflight identified exact NCIt candidates that must be considered before #901's CAS-plus-parent migration under MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3. No record or approval has changed. Fresh-main validation and live issue deduplication are complete: Step 7c merge `467aa319a06ef992035f509f66fe251082b44ae1`; main `467aa319a06ef992035f509f66fe251082b44ae1`, checked `2026-11-03T00:31:09.269512+00:00`; record/hash and mapping-status comparison `all 67 selected source hashes and the named mapping decisions unchanged`; live deduplication `All-state exact term, owner and carbonate-monohydrate queries returned zero hits; all nine maltose matches and their full discussions were reviewed, with no dedicated duplicate.`.\n\nAt inspected C5 `9a8414ad88bbbb01c2a43995e3f0decb2e7f2a7e`, both owners were byte-identical to the preflight's main-derived records:\n\n- `Sodium_Carbonate_Monohydrate.yaml`, SHA256 `6884d4a46259d1e6276a9a83c09079678f0da84c7e468181266115788d316d20`: primary `cas:5968-11-6` with a CLOSE_MATCH parent. Active [NCIT:C80911](https://api-evsrest.nci.nih.gov/api/v1/concept/ncit/C80911?include=full), Sodium Carbonate Monohydrate, has that CAS and formula `CO3.2Na.H2O` and resolves in the installed NCIt database. The archived CultureBotHT source specifies sodium carbonate monohydrate, Sigma S4132, CAS 5968-11-6 and mass 124.\n- `D-Maltose_Monohydrate.yaml`, SHA256 `cda53191390133b9a1059b87938333b4d965e2b9009497dcd7e046af9b1f04d5`: primary `cas:6363-53-7` with CLOSE_MATCH parent CHEBI:17306. Active [NCIT:C80300](https://api-evsrest.nci.nih.gov/api/v1/concept/ncit/C80300?include=full), Maltose Monohydrate, has that CAS and formula `C12H22O11.H2O` and resolves locally. [GSRS DM477EE40D](https://gsrs.ncats.nih.gov/api/v1/substances/DM477EE40D?view=full) links the CAS and NCIt concept to maltose monohydrate. The original source specifies Sigma M5885, D-maltose monohydrate and CAS 6363-53-7. NCIt's beta-maltose names and GSRS's open-chain structural representation require explicit source review before an exact-identity decision.\n\nBounded local and upstream ChEBI searches found no exact candidate for these source forms. The older D-maltose narrative's unsuccessful exact-phrase search does not establish absence from NCIt. Recommend a source-specific ruling on these two candidates before choosing an identifier or predicate. Preserve labels, roles, counts and history; do not merge the generic `Maltose_Hydrate` owner, repurpose a subject or inherit approval. All four mappings were WITHHOLD at the inspected snapshot. #718 role findings remain outside this identity decision.\n\nHistorical deduplication covered #901, #268, #669, #321, #459, #225, #334 and #320, native holds and the D-maltose record review. All-state searches for `maltose`, `C80300`, `C80911` and `carbonate monohydrate` found no dedicated exact-term correction issue. This was a bounded search, not exhaustive manual review; the fresh live result above likewise found no dedicated duplicate.\n\nPrimary response SHA256 values: C80911 `ebcebf0116318aad98e1eb4b0cbb5e5a68f9ffa66eb565d958636f64e82aceac`; C80300 `6f182d2fbb8d52919aecda4a81703d11b04aab9acfa0a3205b1556d0541c85b0`; GSRS maltose `c8815465636c91017c4e104e1ac11d4e5f08702b5bc32a8445c8a36784e3dab0`. Local NCIt database SHA256: `9aac307a33fcf57fb946944a0eaca6029a7d929e29f7522537909da6c71a31d3`.\n\nCompletion requires the source-specific ruling, guarded history-preserving writes, native generated rows and a mapping receipt that adds no approval, withdrawal of stale authority, full native checks and independent final-head review. Broader hydrate and role holds remain intact. The approved plan's unified-snapshot prohibition is a separate unresolved constraint.\n\nFresh evidence ledger: `output/approved-plan-20261101T031134Z/step7d-postmerge-context/FINAL_HANDOFF.json`, SHA256 `f10813a7c8ed96fa443c71d3e6cdf0369a3ddf9548aaf651b62fd75bd7b9f410`. Current owner and mapping readbacks are retained under `step7d-postmerge-467aa319/`; original primary captures and immutable native preflight remain under `step7d-preflight/scientific-preflight/`. This issue grants no scientific approval and has no supervisor or cycle binding.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1117/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1117/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1014","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1014/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1014/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1014/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1014","id":6142088209,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABbhjUEQ","number":1014,"title":"Regenerated carnitine rows drop the #390 provenance comment and switch to new source vocabulary","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-01T01:48:38Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T03:07:22Z","closed_at":"2026-11-01T03:07:21Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Found in an independent adversarial review of #1007 (head `612860e4`). Low–medium.\n\n**Where:** canonical SSSOM, carnitine broadMatch row (position 648), regenerated with claw `d8f95e7e`.\n\n**What happens:**\n- The `[#390 … narrowMatch -> broadMatch …]` provenance comment is dropped. The predicate and `validation_method manual:reconcile_sssom|PREDICATE|2026-09-20` remain, and the sibling `Carnitine_Dl_Hydrochloride` row keeps the same comment (148 such comments become 147).\n- On both carnitine rows, 12 upstream `source` tokens are replaced by new-generator vocabulary. Dropped: `kgm:primary_mappings[chemicals_sssom]`, `[kegg_compound]`, `kgm:chebi_xrefs`, `kgm:culturebotai_reviewed`. Added: `kgm:native_ontology:chebi` and `[manifest=9bb29d56…]`; that manifest hash appears in no committed evidence.\n- These are the only 2 of 2,987 rows using the new vocabulary. The PR hand-kept `DL-carnitine` from the old row but not the comment, and the PR body doesn't mention the drop. The receipt's before-row does keep the old values.\n\n**Suggested fix:** restore the #390 comment. Then either keep the old source tokens for these two rows or document the mixed vocabulary, and commit the manifest evidence.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1014/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1038","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1038/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1038/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1038/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1038","id":6145276392,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABbkl56A","number":1038,"title":"Accept the exact native retained NLDM validation stamp during carnitine promotion","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-01T09:16:44Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T10:42:38Z","closed_at":"2026-11-01T10:42:37Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The first full native #1004 candidate generation exposed an over-strict condition in the unpublished carnitine promotion writer. The guard correctly stopped before any canonical write.\n\nThe merged Claw producer `6a7172585eb68da7f4fe01aee75a82458ddd470c` was run with its supported `--prior-stamps-from` option and the actual original canonical SSSOM. For `MIM:NLDM_metabolites`, the resulting identity/predicate/labels and payload are unchanged; only `source` and `mapping_date` change. The producer correctly retains the prior `validation_method` value `manual:promote_resolved_unmapped|PROMOTED|2026-08-06`. The new writer instead requires an empty value for every selected row, so its dry-run rejects this legitimate unchanged-identity stamp.\n\nReproduction: `output/approved-plan-20261101T031134Z/logs/step3-promotion-dry-run.log`, SHA256 `23bd121fbd29bf5c6fff455a08ce92673480156298df94a685a40228700acdb9`; candidate SHA256 `02b40e540b0663944500071e5725004ec0610e46bf3dd0b83cd4987820af7736`; writer SHA256 `2598d9390087071fcff2a188bd4d4312a935576b8ae4fa15a9239dede7529158`. Source application and synchronization succeeded; canonical SSSOM remains its original bytes.\n\nFix the bounded NLDM expectation to preserve exactly its original stamp when replaying the supported native prior-stamp path. Continue requiring an empty prior stamp for the newly re-grounded NCIT salt row. Reject arbitrary, changed or cross-subject stamps. Add a regression through the actual native prior-stamp carry-forward path, not only the lower-level row constructor, and independently re-review.\n\nThis stamp records historical validation and does not carry scientific release approval. NLDM's changed owner must still be recorded in receipt 17 so its mapping and all 68 component/role approvals are withdrawn by the existing review chain. Do not change that requirement, the NLDM identity, or its other fields. Related to #1004.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1038/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1038/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1176","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1176/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1176/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1176/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1176","id":6267928609,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdZkAIQ","number":1176,"title":"Distinct Neopeptone, Universal and Proteose No.3 products resolve through incompatible peptone owners","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-11-08T05:22:39Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T11:09:54Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The frozen worker05 source review at `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99` found distinct commercial peptones represented as resolving aliases on broader or different owners. This is a source-bound finding against that baseline, not a claim about a later `main` revision.\n\n- `data/ingredients/mapped/Bacto_Peptone.yaml` has three Neopeptone and two Universal peptone aliases. Manufacturer evidence distinguishes [Bacto Peptone 211677](https://www.thermofisher.com/order/catalog/product/211677) from [Neopeptone 211681](https://www.thermofisher.com/order/catalog/product/211681); the latter uses milk protein and animal tissue. [Merck Universal peptone M66](https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/deepweb/assets/sigmaaldrich/product/documents/135/735/107043en-ms.pdf) combines casein, meat and soy peptones. These product distinctions do not support identity to Bacto Peptone.\n- `data/ingredients/mapped/Proteose_Peptone.yaml` has eight numbered No.3 aliases. [Difco Proteose Peptone No.3 211693](https://www.thermofisher.com/order/catalog/product/211693) is separately specified from unnumbered Proteose Peptone 211684 in the [manufacturer technical guide](https://assets.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/BPD/brochures/peptones-supplements-feeds-technical-reference-guide.pdf).\n\nThe exact isolated proposals preserve every raw label/source and change only the specified incompatible aliases to `REJECTED_LABEL`, with new curation events. Generic ambiguous `Peptone mixture` and Oxoid labels are not decided by these product comparisons. Public MICRO:0000177 evidence for Neopeptone is captured, but no new owner or ontology promotion is proposed without the native integration checks.\n\nEvidence and proposed bytes: `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-05/materials/{decisions,evidence,proposals}.json` on `review/all-unmatched-w05-source-review-20261107`. Before hashes: Bacto `864e86820c578ff82b2b32e075c6fb428e704907f78a250c2733b06a70d8e655`; Proteose `c0541faf7f493f617c3f92f8082a1aab6052aa3fa392f802534e201b50ace34e`. Independent chemical reviewer evidence is included in the same worker bundle.\n\nFollow-up: reconcile all campaign proposals touching these owners; use guarded writers; withdraw inherited support for changed payloads; regenerate synchronized exports only during coordinator integration; verify that rejected product labels no longer resolve and that genuine source-qualified product identities remain distinguishable. Keep all existing source, role and export holds. This is separate from #1108's Tryptone/Casamino ownership problem and #883's release freshness issue. Live all-state searches for Neopeptone, Universal peptone and Proteose found no issue covering this product-alias defect; search receipts are in the bundle.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1176/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1254","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1254/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1254/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1254/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1254","id":6270464065,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdb-wQQ","number":1254,"title":"Track corrected final-review packaging and capture metadata","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":13,"created_at":"2026-11-08T11:31:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T15:26:05Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This records three confirmed minor findings in private final-candidate review artifacts. They were recorded by the reviewers before their append-only corrections and independently checked in the completed packets. Coordinator GitHub triage occurs now; it does not claim the fixes waited for this issue. No maintained record, scientific decision, native gate or published source was defective or changed by these corrections.\n\n| Finding | Confirmed problem | Corrected scope and retained evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| W01-HIPO-V2-SEAL-HARNESS-001 | The unexecuted outer seal generator attempted to iterate a science manifest's integer `symlinks: 0` as a list. | A separate successor handles explicit zero counts and actual literal-link lists, verifies the physical ignored-inclusive inventory, and passed independent pre-execution controls. The original generator and all peer manifests remain exact. |\n| W01-HIPO-V2-BINDING-TIME-001 | A draft current-binding report advanced its selector hash to v5 but retained an access timestamp older than content newly added to v5. | The immutable final native pair records the actual selection access time, preserves the prior pair/finding and all scientific assessments, and passed separate native/current-input and skeptical checks. This does not rewrite primary acquisition times. |\n| PEPTONE-ASSEMBLY-META-001 | A review summary attributed one captured Europe PMC response to an equivalent article-ID query rather than its actual DOI query. | The native review-v2 retains the actual acquisition URL, `query=DOI:10.1099/00207713-50-1-107`, for the unchanged captured bytes. The earlier matrix and pair remain preserved; the alternative locator is not claimed as the acquisition request. No new retrieval or source-science change occurred. |\n\nExact evidence under `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/workers/`:\n\n- `w01/worktree/.temp/hipolypepton-v2-independent-v1/`: HANDOFF `27c689e9af0e08e5c864240645ea5c1dd4ab06c7f1f494da1476b1187dc8bad1`, manifest `fb8d95b565903045bd8847a5cba28376b48c22ddc24e9875888be30cd7b2589f`; coordinator verified167 regular members and one literal link. Findings are `findings/W01-HIPO-V2-SEAL-HARNESS-001.json` (`576fbcb982b9e87af728d2cc911f77c05bbab09a924059ab00116833e6fb2e88`) and `findings/W01-HIPO-V2-BINDING-TIME-001.json` (`acc50015c33356e4777f0694b261412ced438ae952eee5a3a316c78a2e1c80d8`). Independent correction evidence is bound by the final handoff.\n- `w10/worktree/.temp/peptone-final-three-independent-v1/`: HANDOFF `263c891884305e85049aba856f91dc967d285d7d275def423e5773bfcf853fe3`, manifest `1e953523faa894d2975ad74650c9d5eab14bcba824d86f7378d2994043150bc3`; coordinator verified1,308 regular members and one literal link. `final-skeptic/metadata-observation-v1.json` is `36db2015e352a086585a25dc515f133baf17fbd0a560892390f10bb1eeedda42`; final review-v2 YAML is `97dc6578b750c098021f164bada00526a0ff22d7f357ce12298aa096baaae0b6`.\n\nThe corresponding scientific findings stay on #1202 and #1233, with component-reference context on #1176. This separate final-review tracker preserves #1159's explicit canary-only scope and #1173's full-shard provenance identity. Remaining work is to carry the exact corrected evidence and its historical lineage into the final campaign publication; no additional source correction or approval is inferred.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1254/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1254/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/765","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/765/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/765/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/765/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/765","id":5566234463,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABS8X_Xw","number":765,"title":"hold_lineage recomputed KGX edge ids from the TSV row, which carries empty optional columns the exporter never hashed","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-09-24T09:28:59Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T19:51:39Z","closed_at":"2026-11-01T19:51:39Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Review finding on #764 (read-only pass), fixed in that PR.\n\n`mapping_change_receipts._edge_id_at` re-derived a mapping edge's `MIM.assertion:` id at its baseline SSSOM position by hashing the edge row as read from `mim_edges.tsv` (minus `id`). But `kgx.Graph.edge` hashes the row it *built*, which for the mapping kind carries only the base columns, while `_write_tsv` emits every `EDGE_COLUMNS` entry, so the TSV row has `publications`, `metabolic_context`, `reference_scope`, `concentration_value`, `concentration_unit`, `completeness` and `assertion_method` as empty strings. Recomputing from the TSV reproduced **0 of 3,026** mapping edge ids on the real bundle, so `hold_lineage` could never match a moved hold and the gate would keep failing on any row removal above position 437 — the failure #745 set out to remove — silently, since an empty lineage just falls back to the exact-id check.\n\nThe unit test caught nothing because it compared against an in-memory `Graph` edge, which has the same key set as the hashed row.\n\nFix (in #764): hash exactly `MAPPING_EDGE_KEYS` (the eleven base columns a mapping edge carries), and add a TSV-shaped case to `tests/test_mapping_change_receipts.py::test_recomputed_ids_match_the_gate_and_the_exporter`. Verified on the real bundle: 3,026 / 3,026 mapping edge ids reproduce at their own position.\n\nNote for anyone extending the lineage to role or component edges: those kinds are created with explicit optional fields, some of them empty strings, so the same recomputation would need the exporter's per-kind field list rather than \"drop empty\".\n\nRelated: #745, #764.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/765/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317","id":5098812922,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABL-m1-g","number":317,"title":"297 records graded EXACT_MATCH are synonym matches; 59 more match nothing in ChEBI","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-08-08T18:12:19Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T05:31:53Z","closed_at":"2026-08-25T05:31:53Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Finding\n\nOf **1,864** records graded `EXACT_MATCH`, **356** carry a CHEBI term whose\nprimary label equals neither the record's `preferred_term` nor any recorded\nsynonym. Resolving each against the local `chebi.db` synonym lists splits them\ncleanly:\n\n| | count | |\n|---|---|---|\n| justified by a ChEBI **synonym** | **297** | term is right, **grade is wrong** |\n| matched by **nothing** in ChEBI (label or synonym) | **59** | needs individual review |\n\n## The 297 are mis-graded by the schema's own definition\n\n`mediaingredientmech.yaml` is unambiguous:\n\n```yaml\nEXACT_MATCH:    Direct exact match to ontology term\nSYNONYM_MATCH:  Matches known synonym in ontology\n```\n\nA label matching a ChEBI *synonym* rather than the primary label is\n`SYNONYM_MATCH` by definition. This is not a judgement call — it is 16% of all\n`EXACT_MATCH` records disagreeing with the enum they use.\n\nThe grade is load-bearing: it is what tells a downstream consumer how much to\ntrust an identity assertion, and `EXACT_MATCH` is the strongest claim available.\n\n## The 59 need review, and are not one thing\n\nSub-classes visible on inspection:\n\n- **Genuine scope loss** — the label carries a qualifier the term does not:\n  `b-Glucan from Oat` → `beta-D-glucan` (source lost),\n  `amylopectin from maize` → `amylopectin`,\n  `Acetate (carbon source)` → `acetate`,\n  `Ammonium chloride (nitrogen source)` → `ammonium chloride`,\n  `Alpha-Toxicarol (Dl)` → `Toxicarol` (racemate → unspecified).\n- **A semantic error** — `Aromatic hydrocarbon` → `polycyclic arene`. Not a\n  synonym relation in either direction: benzene is an aromatic hydrocarbon and\n  is not polycyclic. The term is narrower than the label.\n- **Trivial-vs-systematic naming**, arguably fine but not *exact*:\n  `Butanol` → `butan-1-ol`, `2-Ethylhexanol` → `2-ethylhexan-1-ol`,\n  `2-Piperidinone` → `piperidin-2-one`.\n- **Formula-as-label**: `KNO2` → `potassium nitrite`, `NH42CO3` →\n  `ammonium carbonate`. The formula is not a ChEBI string at all.\n- **Misspellings that nonetheless resolved correctly**:\n  `Pyromelitic acid` → `pyromellitic acid`, `Thioglycollic acid` →\n  `thioglycolic acid`. Compound is right; `EXACT_MATCH` is not.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```python\n# for each EXACT_MATCH record with a CHEBI ontology_id:\n#   skip if preferred_term or a recorded synonym == ontology_label (normalised)\n#   else look up the term's synonyms in ~/.data/oaklib/chebi.db:\n#     any match -> should be SYNONYM_MATCH   (297)\n#     no match  -> review                     (59)\n```\n\nNormalisation is case- and punctuation-insensitive, so this does not flag mere\ncapitalisation differences.\n\n## Suggested action\n\nThe 297 are a safe mechanical re-grade to `SYNONYM_MATCH` with a\n`curation_history` entry — no ontology_id changes, no SSSOM object changes.\nNote the SSSOM predicate may need review alongside it, since `skos:exactMatch`\nrows resting on a synonym match are the same overstatement.\n\nThe 59 need per-record calls; the scope-loss and `Aromatic hydrocarbon` cases\nare real defects, the naming-convention ones probably just want re-grading too.\n\n## Provenance\n\nSurfaced by the Claude research lane, which flagged `EXACT_MATCH` as\nunsupportable on `1-naphtylacetic_Acid`, `5-Hydroxyoctanoate`, `Angustmycin` and\n`Aluminium_Sulfate` independently, then generalised repo-wide against chebi.db.\nRelated: #309, #312, #315, #316.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/453","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/453/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/453/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/453/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/453","id":5242001504,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABOHKYYA","number":453,"title":"Retire or rebuild the public CultureMech bulk importer; current command is schema-invalid and destructive","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10370025893,"node_id":"LA_kwDORhCjFc8AAAACahoJpQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11691350693,"node_id":"LA_kwDORhCjFc8AAAACuNvapQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/labels/needs-human","name":"needs-human","color":"B60205","default":false,"description":"Hard stop for agents. Ontology minting, deletions, schema changes.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11691350822,"node_id":"LA_kwDORhCjFc8AAAACuNvbJg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/labels/high_effort","name":"high_effort","color":"F9D0C4","default":false,"description":"Open-ended or risky. Routed to the strongest model.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-08-25T04:16:52Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T06:27:03Z","closed_at":"2026-08-25T06:27:03Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\n`just import-data` is still advertised as the supported CultureMech intake path, but its implementation is a zombie command rather than a safe current workflow.\n\nAgainst the current CultureMech output (1,004 mapped rows), `scripts/import_from_culturemech.py` aborts closed-schema validation with 2,008 errors: every mapped record writes the retired root `ontology_id` field and omits required `identifier`. The surviving corpus has 616 `import_from_culturemech` history events, all at the same March 2026 timestamp, consistent with a one-time seed rather than a maintained updater.\n\nMore importantly, simply fixing that key would reactivate a destructive full overwrite:\n\n- `import_mapped()` and `import_unmapped()` replace both curated collection files;\n- existing curation, roles, history, local identifiers, and review decisions are not merged;\n- `docs/WORKFLOWS.md` nevertheless says re-import preserves curation history and makes new ingredients unmapped;\n- README, the justfile, and agent skill references still recommend the command.\n\nThis was found while preventing recurrence of #317. That branch now translates CultureMech's generic `DIRECT_MATCH` default conservatively instead of silently minting MIM `EXACT_MATCH`, but it deliberately does not reactivate this broader import path.\n\n## Scope\n\nMake an explicit lifecycle decision:\n\n1. **Retire now:** remove/disable the public `import-data` recipe and correct every maintained doc/agent reference until a safe replacement exists; or\n2. **Rebuild:** implement a validated, merge-safe, deterministic intake path that preserves MIM-owned curation and reports conflicts before writing.\n\nDo not make the current script appear operational by changing only `ontology_id` to `identifier`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The public command surface cannot invoke a schema-invalid or destructive overwrite by accident.\n- [ ] README, `docs/WORKFLOWS.md`, `scripts/README.md`, and maintained agent references agree on supported status.\n- [ ] If retained, converted mapped and unmapped records validate against the current closed schema.\n- [ ] Existing MIM-owned fields and curation history survive an update; target changes are conflict-reviewed and provenance-recorded.\n- [ ] Failure is atomic: no curated collection is replaced after only one half succeeds.\n- [ ] Import tests cover current identifiers, preservation of existing curation, new rows, removed rows, and target conflicts.\n- [ ] Mapping quality remains evidence-based per #317; CultureMech `DIRECT_MATCH` must not become MIM `EXACT_MATCH` without preserved match-method evidence.\n- [ ] Recipe-reference and occurrence handling align with #447 and #449 rather than cementing the current name-only/capped contract.\n\n## Dependencies / related\n\n- #317: mapping-quality provenance guard (independent, can land first).\n- #447: stable typed CultureMech recipe references.\n- #449: lossless recipe memberships and correct `media_count`.\n- `scripts/merge_culturemech_updates.py` is explicitly historical under `scripts/README.md`; it is not a substitute for a maintained intake command.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/453/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/453/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/127","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/127/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/127/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/127/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/127","id":4925302839,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABJZIoNw","number":127,"title":"OSMOTIC_AGENT and OSMOPROTECTANT both map to CHEBI:25728 — needs curator guidance to prevent auto-classifier double-assignment","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-20T02:34:16Z","updated_at":"2026-07-20T04:20:06Z","closed_at":"2026-07-20T04:20:06Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Discovered during code review of #121.\n\n`PhysicochemicalRoleEnum.OSMOTIC_AGENT` and `CellularMetabolicRoleEnum.OSMOPROTECTANT` both use `mappings: - CHEBI:25728` (osmolyte). Both mappings are legitimate (osmolyte covers both concepts in CHEBI), but any downstream auto-labeler that fans out CHEBI → schema will double-assign every osmolyte-annotated ingredient to both facets, defeating the point of separating them.\n\n**Failure scenario:** An auto-classifier reading `CHEBI:25728` in the MIM SSSOM assigns the same compound to both `PhysicochemicalRoleEnum.OSMOTIC_AGENT` and `CellularMetabolicRoleEnum.OSMOPROTECTANT` without organism context — a spurious dual-assignment.\n\n**Fix:** in the follow-up PR that adds the assignment classes/slots + curator writer methods, either (a) add validator logic that requires organism context before `OSMOPROTECTANT` is assigned, or (b) add curator-facing guidance in the schema descriptions. **No schema change needed for #121.**","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/127/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/127/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/192","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/192/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/192/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/192/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/192","id":5056447934,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABLWNFvg","number":192,"title":"Review the 386 PENDING_REVIEW microbedecoder auto-groundings before they reach the SSSOM","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-08-04T03:42:02Z","updated_at":"2026-08-04T07:25:25Z","closed_at":"2026-08-04T07:25:25Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Outstanding curation from the microbedecoder onboarding (kg-microbe `data/transformed/microbedecoder/unmapped_labels.tsv`).\n\nThe import auto-grounded 403 labels via `ols-label-exact-chebi` / `-ncit`. Rather than publish those on automated label matching alone, they are held at **`mapping_status: PENDING_REVIEW`** — the schema's own \"Suggested mapping awaiting review\". `reconcile_sssom.py` only publishes `MAPPED` records, so they are structurally barred from the published SSSOM until a reviewer flips the status.\n\n- **386** at `PENDING_REVIEW` awaiting review\n- **17** already rejected by the blocking id↔label gate and demoted to `UNMAPPED` (see below)\n- Manifest: `reports/microbedecoder_auto_mapped_review.tsv` — one row per record with `ontology_id`, `ontology_label`, resolver method, and a `review_verdict` column\n\n## Why this is not a rubber stamp\n\nThe gate rejected **17 of 403 (4%)** outright: CHEBI accessions above the 300000 ceiling in `conf/id_label_targets.yaml` that do not resolve in the local ChEBI adapter — `CHEBI:759086` (polymyxin B), `CHEBI:756054` (carbomycin), `CHEBI:759883` (colistin sulfate), `CHEBI:759884` (gentamicin), `CHEBI:753395` (lysostaphin), `CHEBI:748901` (netilmicin), and 11 more. **All antibiotics**, which suggests a systematic resolver problem on that class rather than scattered bad luck — worth checking whether the remaining antibiotic groundings in the 386 share it.\n\nThat is the same signature as this repo's earlier incidents: a PubChem CID wearing a `CHEBI:` prefix, and `CHEBI:86457` standing in for \"MnCl·4H₂O\".\n\n## Suggested approach\n\n`review-ingredients` over the manifest, prioritising:\n\n1. The antibiotic rows, given 100% of the rejected ids were antibiotics.\n2. Rows whose `ontology_label` differs from `preferred_term` by more than case — an exact-label match that needed normalising is where a homonym slips through.\n3. Everything else in bulk.\n\nFlip reviewed records to `MAPPED`, then `python scripts/reconcile_sssom.py --apply --date <YYYY-MM-DD>` publishes only those.\n\nBlocked on nothing. Depends on #191 only in the sense that any further import should not be run until the write-back is fixed.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/192/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/192/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/321","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/321/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/321/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/321/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/321","id":5098973408,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABL-wo4A","number":321,"title":"26 hydrate-named records map to anhydrous terms; 10 terms absorb multiple distinct hydrates","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2026-08-08T18:55:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T05:41:49Z","closed_at":"2026-09-11T19:27:00Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## The check\n\nFlag any record whose `preferred_term` names a hydrate (`x n H2O`, `·nH2O`,\n`hydrate`) while its recorded formula/SMILES/InChI contain **no water\ncomponent**. Purely mechanical.\n\n**Result: 26 records.**\n\n## Why the existing CAS-vs-structure check cannot see this\n\nBoth compared fields are populated from the same ChEBI term by\n`AUTO_BACKFILL_CHEBI_CHEMISTRY`, so they agree **by construction**. The check\ncompares the record against itself; the *label* is the only field carrying the\ncontradicting information, and nothing was comparing against it.\n\n## The sharper pattern: one term absorbing many distinct hydrates\n\n**10 ontology terms carry 26 distinct hydrate labels between them:**\n\n| term | absorbs |\n|---|---|\n| CHEBI:34683 | `Na2HPO4 x 2/3/6/7/12 H2O` — **five** different hydrates |\n| CHEBI:35696 | `CoCl2 x 2/4/6 H2O` |\n| CHEBI:34887 | `NiCl2 x 2/5/6 H2O` |\n| CHEBI:75832 | `FeSO4 x 5/6/7 H2O` |\n| CHEBI:23414 | `CuSO4 x 2/4 H2O` |\n| CHEBI:30812 | `FeCl2 x 6/7 H2O` |\n| CHEBI:86360 | `MnSO4 x 1/7 H2O` |\n| CHEBI:53001 | `NiSO4 x 6/7 H2O` |\n\nDifferent hydrates are different substances with different formula weights and\ndifferent CAS numbers. Collapsed onto one term they are indistinguishable\ndownstream — a recipe calling for the heptahydrate and one calling for the\ndihydrate become the same node.\n\n**The assignment is demonstrably arbitrary.** Magnesium sulfate splits across two\nterms *by notation rather than by chemistry*:\n\n```\nCHEBI:32599  <- \"MgSO4 x 6 H2O\",  \"MgSO4·7H2O\"\nCHEBI:31795  <- \"MgSO4 x 7 H2O\",  \"MgSO4·H2O\"\n```\n\nThe **same** hydration number (7) lands on two different terms depending on\nwhether the label was written `x 7 H2O` or `·7H2O`. That is lexical matching\nwith no chemistry behind it.\n\nOne record states the contradiction outright: `Na2-EDTA x 2 H2O` carries\n`ontology_label: EDTA disodium salt (anhydrous)`.\n\n## Triage forks three ways — do not mass-apply\n\nEstablished from three worked cases:\n\n1. **The label is wrong.** `CaSO4 x 7 H2O` — no calcium sulfate heptahydrate\n   exists (ChEBI has anhydrous/hemi/dihydrate only). Probably a `2`→`7` slip,\n   but confirming needs the source recipes read. MediaDive maps\n   `CaSO4 x 2 H2O` correctly, so it does distinguish these when they are real.\n2. **The label is right and the ontology is deficient.** `CeCl3 x 7 H2O` is the\n   standard commercial form; ChEBI has **no** cerium chloride hydrate at all.\n   Ignoring the waters here is a **51% formula-weight error** (246 → 373).\n   Candidate for a registry term.\n3. **Neither side is definite.** `Cefsulodin sodium salt hydrate` — no hydrate\n   term in any ontology *and* the label states no hydration number. Nothing to\n   encode; the fix is dropping `EXACT_MATCH` and recording why.\n\nSo a lexical `x n H2O` sweep would fix (1) and corrupt (2).\n\n## Suggested action\n\nAdd the detector as a standing check, then triage the 26 by the fork above.\nThe `Na2HPO4` five-way and `CoCl2`/`NiCl2` three-way collapses are the highest\nvalue — they are the cases where distinct media ingredients have become\nindistinguishable.\n\n## Provenance\n\nDetector proposed by the Claude research lane after the CAS-vs-structure check\npassed on three defective records in one batch, with the correct diagnosis of\nwhy it structurally could not catch them. Verified repo-wide.\nRelated: #315, #317, #320.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/321/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/321/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}